      "narrative": "Critical Loop, a Series A-stage climate and energy technology company founded by Bala Ramamurthy, has raised $49M to date. The valuation assessment draws on a comparative universe of nine same-sector peers, including one public company (LNZA) and eight private firms such as Helion, Redwood Materials, QuantumScape, KoBold Metals, and Electric Hydrogen.\n\nGiven the absence of sufficient same-stage and adjacent-stage comparable data within Climate & Energy, the peer-median method was not applicable; a broader cross-sector median would introduce unacceptable bias. Instead, valuation relies on stage-progression methodology, which applies a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A advancement to the $49M total capital deployed as a proxy floor. This yields an implied valuation of $98M.\n\nThe triangulated analysis, constrained to one applicable method, supports a range of $83M (low) to $113M (high), with a median of $98M. The primary uncertainty stems from the limited dataset\u2014the Climate & Energy sector lacks granular peer comparables at Critical Loop's stage, making any single-method conclusion more sensitive to multiplier assumptions. Additional conviction would require either identifying additional same-stage private comparables or observing transaction data from nearer peers. The $98M median should be treated as directional pending further market evidence.",
