      "narrative": "Auriga Space is a Series A frontier-tech company in Space & Aerospace that has raised $12.2M to date. The valuation exercise draws on a comp universe of 5 public peers (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private peers including SpaceX, Sierra Space, and Planet Labs, though narrow-filter peer multiples proved insufficient for reliable median-based triangulation.\n\nOf the three methods tested, only stage-progression anchoring proved applicable. Using total capital raised ($12.2M) as a valuation proxy and applying a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A to subsequent-stage progression yields an implied valuation of $24M. Peer-median comparison was not viable due to insufficient same-stage and adjacent-stage comps within Space & Aerospace meeting minimum sample thresholds (found 0 same-stage, 2 adjacent-stage peers). Public-comp P/S anchoring, while the sector median trades at 23.9x revenue across five public names, could not be applied without Auriga's revenue figure, which remains undisclosed.\n\nThe single applicable method supports a valuation range of $21M (low) to $28M (high), with a median of $24M. This estimate carries material uncertainty given reliance on a single methodological input and the absence of comparable Series A transactions in the immediate peer set. Revenue disclosure or disclosure of recent comparable private fundraising would materially strengthen conviction in this range.",
