      "narrative": "Twenty is a Series A-stage Defense & Security company that has raised $38M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a peer universe of 10 comparable companies in the same sector and stage cohort, comprising 8 private firms and 2 public comparables (DRSHF, IDEAFORGE.NS). Key private peers include Singularity, NODA AI, Anduril Industries, Helsing, and Shield AI, which collectively span Series B valuations from $1.0B to $3.0B.\n\nTwo valuation methods were applied. Stage-progression, using total capital raised as a proxy, applies a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A advancement, yielding $76M. The peer-median approach references the $1.0B median valuation across the 10-company comparison set (range: $125M\u2013$3.0B), reflecting predominantly Series B-stage peers trading at higher multiples. This divergence reflects both Twenty's earlier stage and the marked scaling observed within Defense & Security over recent rounds.\n\nTriangulation of these methods produces a valuation range of $65M (low) to $1.1B (high), with a median of $538M. The wide dispersion reflects material uncertainty around Twenty's competitive positioning relative to later-stage cohort members and the limited early-stage Defense & Security data points. Key sensitivities include revenue traction, customer concentration, and near-term capital requirements. Stage-progression anchors the downside; peer comparables establish ceiling dynamics absent significant differentiation metrics.",
