      "narrative": "Shield AI, a Series G defense and security company, is valued at $12.7B post-money following $1.5B+ in cumulative funding. The valuation is assessed against a peer universe of 10 comparable companies (2 public, 8 private) operating in the Defense & Security sector, including Anduril Industries, Helsing, Saronic, and Flock Safety.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. The stage-progression method uses Shield AI's current $12.7B valuation as a baseline and applies a 1.25x step-up multiplier typical of progression from Series G to the next financing stage, implying $15.9B. The peer-median method evaluates eight same-sector competitors at similar valuation tiers, yielding a median valuation of $7.8B, with a range spanning $3.0B to $61.0B\u2014the latter driven by Anduril Industries at Series H ($61.0B).\n\nTriangulation across these two methods produces a low estimate of $6.6B, a median of $11.8B, and a high estimate of $18.3B. The current $12.7B post-money valuation falls within this range near the median, suggesting fair value alignment. Key uncertainties include the wide dispersion within the peer set\u2014a 20x spread between minimum and maximum\u2014and stage heterogeneity across comparables, which limits precision. The peer-median approach is conservative relative to stage-progression, reflecting both valuation maturity risk and the company's position within a volatile and unevenly-valued sector.",
