      "narrative": "Castelion, a Series B defense and security company founded by Bryon Hargis, Sean Pitt, and Andrew Kreitz, is evaluated against a comparable universe of 10 firms (2 public, 8 private) operating in the same sector and stage. The peer set spans valuations from $300M to $3.0B, with a median of $1.1B.\n\nTwo triangulation methods apply to this valuation. Stage-progression analysis applies a 1.9x step-up multiplier to the company's last post-money valuation of $1.0B, implying $1.9B. Peer-median analysis references six same-sector, same-stage comparables with a median valuation of $1.1B, grounding the lower end of the range. The peer cohort includes Dream Security ($3.0B), Harmattan AI ($1.4B), Code Metal ($1.2B), Defense Unicorns ($1.0B), and Heven AeroTech ($1.0B).\n\nSynthesizing both methods yields a valuation range of $956M (low) to $2.2B (high), with a median of $1.5B. This range reflects the wide dispersion within the peer set\u2014a 10x spread between minimum and maximum\u2014which introduces material uncertainty around appropriate positioning within Defense & Security at Series B. The stage-progression multiple and peer median provide anchoring, though the outlier valuations (particularly Dream Security at $3.0B) suggest heterogeneity in how market participants price companies at this stage. Key uncertainties include relative product maturity, revenue traction, and customer concentration relative to the peer cohort.",
