      "narrative": "Skydio, a Series F autonomous systems provider in Defense & Security, carries a last post-money valuation of $4.4B following $825M+ in total capital raised. The company is evaluated against a peer set of 16 private and public Defense & Security firms at similar valuation tiers, including publicly traded comparables (DRSHF, IDEAFORGE.NS) and established private competitors such as Helsing ($18.0B, Series D), Shield AI ($12.7B, Series G), and Saronic ($9.2B, Series D).\n\nTwo valuation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, anchored to Skydio's $4.4B Series F post-money valuation with a typical 1.3x step-up multiplier to the next funding stage, implies a forward valuation of $5.7B. Peer-median triangulation across 16 same-sector comparables yields a median valuation of $2.2B, with a peer range spanning $1.0B to $18.0B. The dispersion reflects significant variation within the Defense & Security venture cohort.\n\nSynthesizing both methods produces a triangulated valuation range of $1.8B (low) to $6.6B (high), with a median of $3.9B. The $4.4B current valuation sits in the upper-middle of this range, slightly below the stage-progression estimate but substantially above peer median. Key uncertainties include the timing and scale of Skydio's progression to Series G, margin trajectory in autonomous systems, and regulatory and export restrictions specific to defense-tech valuations.",
