      "narrative": "Vannevar Labs is a Series B defense and security technology company that has raised $90M to date. The valuation assessment draws on a comparable universe of 10 peers\u20142 public companies (DRSHF, IDEAFORGE.NS) and 8 private firms operating in the same sector and stage. The primary private comp set includes Dream Security ($3.0B), Harmattan AI ($1.4B), Code Metal ($1.2B), Castelion ($1.0B), and Defense Unicorns ($1.0B).\n\nTwo triangulation methods prove applicable. Stage-progression analysis applies a 1.9x step-up multiplier to the $90M total capital raised, yielding $171M. This method assumes typical venture advancement mechanics but relies on raised capital as a valuation proxy rather than direct financial performance. Peer-median analysis across 7 same-sector, same-stage comparables produces a $1.0B implied value, with the peer range spanning $300M to $3.0B. The wide dispersion reflects heterogeneity in revenue traction, customer concentration, and perceived defensibility within the defense tech segment.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $145M (low) to $1.1B (high), with a median estimate of $586M. The substantial gap between stage-progression ($171M) and peer-median ($1.0B) reflects uncertainty around Vannevar's relative positioning on metrics like ARR, gross margins, and customer quality versus the comp set. Key sensitivities include stage-specific funding conditions, actual revenue run rate relative to peers, and investor risk appetite for defense-sector concentration.",
