      "narrative": "General Matter is a Series A nuclear energy company founded by Scott Nolan and Lee Robinson that has raised $50M+. The valuation analysis draws on a sector peer set comprising 3 public companies (OKLO, NNE, SMR) and 8 private firms including Fuse Energy, X-Energy, and Nano Nuclear Energy.\n\nA stage-progression methodology was applied, using the $50M total raised as a valuation proxy and applying a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical for Series A progression to the next financing stage. This method yielded an implied valuation of $100M. A peer-median approach was not applicable; while 4 nuclear energy peers exist in the broader comp universe, fewer than 3 same-stage or adjacent-stage comparables with similar valuation tier could be isolated to generate a reliable median. Relying on an all-sector median would introduce excessive noise and was therefore excluded.\n\nThe single-method triangulation supports a valuation range of $85M to $115M, with a median of $100M. This range reflects reasonable bounds around the stage-progression result given typical Series A volatility. Key uncertainties include the lack of narrow-peer validation\u2014a broader peer set could refine estimates\u2014and the reliance on total raised as a valuation proxy rather than disclosed post-money terms. Investors should seek disclosure of previous round post-money valuations and comparable transaction data within the advanced nuclear subsector to narrow this range.",
