      "narrative": "Palantir operates in the AI & Software sector as a publicly traded company with a current market capitalization of $312.5 billion, having raised over $3 billion in pre-IPO funding. The comparable universe for valuation is constrained: the sector contains 15 same-sector peers total, but only 1 public comparable (Palantir itself) and 8 private peers identified, including Waymo, Figure AI, Scale AI, Reflection AI, and Applied Intuition. The narrow peer set reflects the nascent stage and heterogeneity of frontier AI infrastructure.\n\nStandard peer-median methodology is inapplicable here due to insufficient comparable depth. Filtering for same-stage, adjacent-stage, or similar-valuation-tier peers yielded fewer than three datapoints, the minimum threshold for reliable median estimation. A sector-wide median would obscure rather than inform, given the wide dispersion in business models, revenue maturity, and strategic positioning across the 15 AI & Software names.\n\nWithout sufficient comparable transactions or a dense peer cohort, triangulated valuation synthesis cannot be meaningfully constructed from market data alone. The current $312.5B public market valuation stands as the only definitive anchor. Further valuation work would require either: expansion to looser sector peers at risk of reduced relevance, or reliance on alternative methods such as discounted cash flow modeling or precedent transaction analysis\u2014neither of which are supported by the data provided here. Key uncertainties center on whether current public valuation reflects sustainable frontier-AI economics or residual momentum from the 2023\u20132024 AI cycle.",
