      "narrative": "Senra Systems is a Series A robotics and manufacturing company that has raised $40M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a peer universe of 9 private robotics firms and 1 public comparable, providing triangulation across stage-matched and sector-aligned reference points.\n\nTwo valuation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis applies a 2.0x step-up multiplier to the $40M total raised, implying $80M. Peer-median analysis benchmarks against three same-sector, same/adjacent-stage companies: Bedrock Robotics ($1.8B Series B), Dexterity ($1.6B Series B), and Walden Robotics ($1.1B Seed). The median of this peer set is $1.6B, with a range of $1.1B to $1.8B.\n\nThe triangulated analysis across both methods supports a valuation range of $68M (low) to $1.9B (high), with a median of $865M. The wide spread reflects inherent tension between stage-based metrics anchored to capital deployed and peer-relative positioning within a sector showing substantial valuation dispersion. Key uncertainties include stage-timing assumptions embedded in the 2.0x multiplier and the heterogeneity of peer capital efficiency and market timing. The peer set spans Seed through Series B, introducing stage-mixing risk. Resolution of this range will depend on Senra's demonstrated customer traction, capital efficiency metrics relative to the peer cohort, and forward fundraising environment.",
