      "narrative": "Atom Bodies is a Series A-stage biotech company founded by Tyler Hayes, Doug Satzger, and Eric Monsef, having raised $2M+ to date. The valuation analysis draws on a peer universe of 3 public companies in Biotech & Health (RXRX, TEM, ONT.L) and 8 private peers including Colossal Biosciences, Abridge, and Recursion Pharmaceuticals.\n\nOf three valuation methods examined, only stage-progression proved applicable. Using the $2M total raised as a valuation proxy and applying a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical for Series A advancement, the method implies a $4M valuation. Peer-median analysis could not be executed: while 8 same-sector peers exist, filtering for matching stage, adjacency, or valuation tier yielded fewer than 3 datapoints, making sector-wide medians unreliable. Public-comp anchoring via P/S multiples (5.5x median across the three public tickers) is not applicable without Atom Bodies' disclosed revenue, which is unavailable for private companies.\n\nThe triangulation supports a valuation range of $3M to $5M, with $4M as the median point. This range reflects conservative ($3M) to moderate ($5M) positioning relative to Series A stage norms. Key uncertainties include the absence of direct comparable transactions at identical stage and the lack of revenue or unit-economics data necessary for multiple-based methods. A fuller valuation would benefit from proprietary financial metrics and founder traction indicators not present in this dataset.",
