      "narrative": "Mammoth Biosciences is a Series D-stage biotech company founded by Jennifer Doudna and co-founders, having raised $600M+ to date. Valuation triangulation draws on two applicable methods across a comp universe of 4 private peers in Biotech & Health at Series C\u2013E stages: Colossal Biosciences ($10.3B Series C), Abridge ($5.3B Series E), Chai Discovery ($3.8B Series C), and New Limit ($3.1B Series C). Public comparables (RXRX, TEM, ONT.L) exist but cannot be applied due to lack of target revenue disclosure.\n\nThe Stage-Progression method applies a 1.5x step-up multiplier to the $600M capital proxy, yielding $900M. The Peer-Median method anchors to the $4.5B median valuation across the four same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comps (range: $3.1B\u2013$10.3B). Public-comp P/S anchoring is inapplicable given revenue is not on file for this private company.\n\nThese two methods triangulate to a range of $765M (low) to $5.2B (high), with a median of $2.7B. The wide range reflects meaningful dispersion in recent frontier biotech valuations; Stage-Progression implies a more conservative floor tied directly to capital deployed, while Peer-Median captures recent market pricing of similarly-staged life science companies. Key uncertainties include the company's clinical stage, underlying asset risk profile, and whether recent peer valuations reflect durable market conditions or transient capital availability.",
