      "narrative": "Base Power, a Series C climate and energy company founded by Zach Dell and Justin Lopas, is evaluated against a peer universe of 8 private companies and 1 public comparable ( Linza: LNZA). The three most directly comparable private peers\u2014KoBold Metals, Electric Hydrogen, and Amogy\u2014all operate in the same sector at the same stage.\n\nTwo valuation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis uses Base Power's $1.0B total raised as a proxy and applies a 1.7x step-up multiplier typical of Series C advancement, implying a $1.7B valuation. Peer-median analysis of the three same-stage, same-sector comparables yields a median valuation of $1.0B, with a range of $700M to $3.0B. The wide peer dispersion reflects heterogeneous technology maturity and market positioning within the frontier energy cohort.\n\nTriangulating these methods produces a valuation range of $850M to $2.0B, with a median of $1.4B. This implies a modest step-up from total capital deployed, consistent with late-stage funding dynamics in capital-intensive sectors. Key uncertainties include the stage definition of peer companies\u2014whether peers represent true Series C equivalents\u2014and the applicability of public comps given frontier-tech illiquidity and execution risk. Downside risk concentrates around pre-commercial validation; upside hinges on regulatory clarity and near-term capital efficiency metrics.",
