      "narrative": "Extropic, a Series A\u2013stage semiconductor company founded by Guillaume Verdon and Trevor McCourt, has raised $50M+ to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comp universe of 11 private and public firms in the Chips & Semiconductors sector, including public peers Nvidia, AMD, and Altium (ALAB), alongside private-stage companies such as SambaNova Systems, Cerebras, and Etched.\n\nStage-progression methodology is the primary applicable valuation approach. Using total capital raised of $50M as a proxy for current enterprise value and applying a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A to later-stage progression, the method implies a valuation of $100M. A peer-median approach could not be reliably applied; while the broader sector contains 11 comparable firms, the narrow filter of same-stage and similar-tier companies yielded fewer than the three datapoints required for statistical confidence, and a broader sectoral median would obscure material differences in business model and technology maturity.\n\nThe triangulated valuation range is $85M (low) to $115M (high), with a median of $100M. This analysis rests on a single method, creating material reliance on the stage-progression assumption. Key uncertainties include the trajectory of technology adoption, competitive positioning within a crowded frontier-chip landscape, and path-to-revenue timing\u2014factors that will materially influence next-round pricing.",
