      "narrative": "Albedo is a Series B-stage space and aerospace company that has raised $130M+ to date. The valuation analysis draws on a peer universe of five private companies at Series B/C stage (Sierra Space at $8.0B, Cowboy Space Corporation at $2.0B, Varda Space Industries at $1.5B, Aalyria at $1.3B, and Skyryse at $1.1B) and six public comparables in the Space & Aerospace sector.\n\nTwo quantitative methods prove applicable. Stage-progression analysis, using the $130M raised as a valuation proxy and applying a typical Series B step-up multiplier of 1.9x, yields $247M. Peer-median analysis across the five same-sector, same/adjacent-stage companies produces a median valuation of $1.5B, with a range spanning $1.1B to $8.0B. Public-comp anchoring via P/S multiple cannot be applied absent disclosed revenue data. Public comparables show a median EV/Sales of 23.9x across six traded tickers, but this method remains unusable for a private company without revenue.\n\nThe triangulation of applicable methods supports a valuation range of $210M (low) to $1.7B (high), with a median of $874M. The wide dispersion reflects genuine uncertainty: stage-progression suggests a more conservative $247M, while peer medians anchor substantially higher at $1.5B. Key uncertainties include revenue trajectory, competitive differentiation within the crowded space-tech sector, and whether Albedo's technology and market position align with higher-valued peers like Sierra Space or lower-valued ones like Aalyria.",
