      "narrative": "Astrolab is a Series A-stage space and aerospace company that has raised $40M+ to date. The valuation exercise draws on a sector universe of 6 public comparables (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private peers including SpaceX, Sierra Space, and Planet Labs, though narrower same-stage filtering yielded insufficient datapoints for robust peer-median triangulation.\n\nThe stage-progression method is the primary applicable approach here. Using total raised ($40M) as a valuation proxy and applying a standard 2.0x step-up multiplier to reflect progression from Series A to subsequent rounds yields an implied valuation of $80M. The peer-median method could not be reliably applied due to insufficient comparables meeting the same-stage and valuation-tier criteria within the Space & Aerospace sector. Public-comp anchoring via price-to-sales multiples (sector median 23.9x across five tickers) is not viable absent disclosed revenue figures for the target.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $68M to $92M, centered on $80M. This narrow range reflects reliance on a single methodological pillar. Key uncertainties include the actual revenue run-rate and unit economics relative to public-market peers, near-term customer wins or government contracts that could materially shift growth expectations, and execution risk inherent to early-stage aerospace ventures. A more diversified conclusion would require either disclosed financials or a larger cohort of same-stage private comparables.",
