      "narrative": "Armada is a Series B space and aerospace company founded by Dan Wright and Jon Runyan that has raised $186M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a comparison universe of five private peers at same or adjacent stages (Sierra Space, Cowboy Space Corporation, Varda Space Industries, Aalyria, and Skyryse) and six public space and aerospace companies (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL, and one additional ticker).\n\nTwo valuation methods proved applicable. Stage-progression analysis, using total capital raised as a proxy for current value, applies a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical of Series B progression, implying a valuation of $353M. Peer-median anchoring across the five same-sector, same/adjacent-stage private comparables yields a median valuation of $1.5B, with a range of $1.1B to $8.0B. Public-comp anchoring via price-to-sales multiples (median 23.9x across the six tickers) could not be applied due to the absence of revenue disclosure for the target.\n\nThe triangulation of these two applicable methods produces a valuation range of $300M (low) to $1.7B (high), with a median of $927M. The substantial gap between stage-progression and peer-median results reflects the wide dispersion in private aerospace valuations at this stage. Key uncertainties include Armada's revenue trajectory relative to peers and the relevance of the peer set, which spans valuations from $1.1B to $8.0B.",
