      "narrative": "Agility Robotics, a Series D robotics and manufacturing company that has raised $400M+, is evaluated against a comparable universe of 9 private firms and 1 public company in the sector. The peer set includes four directly comparable companies: Divergent (Series E, $2.3B), Exotec (Series D, $2.0B), Hadrian (Series C, $1.6B), and Nimble Robotics (Series C, $1.0B).\n\nTwo valuation methods were applied. The stage-progression method uses the $5.2B implied by total capital raised as a baseline and applies a 1.5x step-up multiplier typical for Series D advancement, yielding $7.8B. The peer-median method identifies a $1.8B median valuation across the four comparable companies, with a range of $1.0B to $2.3B. The peer approach reflects market pricing for robotics companies at similar development stages.\n\nThe triangulated analysis produces a median estimate of $4.8B with a low of $1.5B and a high of $9.0B. The wide range reflects material tension between the two methods: the stage-progression approach anchors to deployment of capital raised, while peer-median reflects observed market valuations for comparable Series C/D robotics firms. Key uncertainties include the sustainability of the $5.2B raised-capital baseline as a forward valuation proxy and whether Agility's technology differentiation justifies a premium or discount relative to the peer cohort.",
