      "narrative": "Re:Build Manufacturing is a Series A robotics and manufacturing company founded by Miles Arnone, Jeff Wilke, Anthony Manzo, and Michael Foley. The valuation analysis draws on a comparable universe of 9 private companies and 1 public firm (277810.KQ) operating in the same sector and stage band.\n\nTwo valuation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, using the company's $545M total capital raised as a proxy baseline, applies a 2.0x multiplier typical for Series A progression to the next funding stage, yielding $1.1B. Peer-median analysis across three same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables\u2014Bedrock Robotics ($1.8B Series B), Dexterity ($1.6B Series B), and Walden Robotics ($1.1B Seed)\u2014produces a median valuation of $1.6B, with a range of $1.1B to $1.8B.\n\nThe triangulated analysis across both methods supports a valuation range of $926M to $1.9B, with a median of $1.4B. The stage-progression method anchors the lower bound, while peer median sits in the middle of the range. Key uncertainties include the representativeness of the three-peer set given heterogeneous stages within the comparable cohort, and the appropriateness of using total capital raised as a valuation proxy absent current financial metrics or explicit prior round pricing.",
