      "narrative": "AMP Robotics, a Series A robotics and manufacturing company founded by Matanya Horowitz that has raised $180M+, is valued against a comp universe of nine private firms and one public entity. The private comps include Bedrock Robotics ($1.8B Series B), Dexterity ($1.6B Series B), and Walden Robotics ($1.1B Seed), among others in the robotics sector.\n\nTwo valuation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, using total raised as a proxy base of $30M and applying a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical for Series A advancement, implied a $60M valuation. Peer-median analysis across three same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables yielded a median valuation of $1.6B, with a range of $1.1B to $1.8B. The peer method carries materially greater weight given the availability of direct stage and sector matches.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $51M (low) to $1.9B (high), with a median of $855M. The wide spread reflects tension between the stage-progression method, which anchors to capital raised, and peer multiples, which embed market-clearing valuations for later-stage robotics companies. Key uncertainties include AMP's relative unit economics versus listed peers, revenue traction relative to capital deployed, and whether the Series B comparables appropriately discount for AMP's current stage and operational maturity.",
