      "narrative": "Science Corporation is a Series B biotech company founded by Max Hodak that has raised $230M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a comparable universe of 8 private peers and 3 public companies in Biotech & Health, including Series B and Series C-stage firms such as Eikon Therapeutics ($539M), Chai Discovery ($3.8B), Colossal Biosciences ($10.3B), and New Limit ($3.1B).\n\nTwo valuation methods apply. Stage-progression analysis uses the $230M raised as a proxy base value and applies a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical for Series B advancement, yielding $437M. Peer-median analysis across the 4 same-sector comparable companies produces a median valuation of $3.5B, with a range spanning $539M to $10.3B. Public-comp anchoring cannot be applied due to absence of revenue data, though the median public sector multiple is 5.5x P/S across RXRX, TEM, and ONT.L.\n\nThe triangulation of applicable methods supports a valuation range of $371M (low) to $4.0B (high), with a median of $1.9B. The wide dispersion reflects material uncertainty around Science Corporation's position relative to the peer set\u2014particularly whether its profile aligns with earlier-stage peers like Eikon Therapeutics or more mature Series C entrants. Investor conviction on clinical/commercial progress and capital efficiency will be decisive in narrowing this range.",
