      "narrative": "Asylon Robotics is a Series B-stage drone and autonomous systems company that has raised $40M to date. The relevant peer universe in Drones & Autonomous comprises eight private companies\u2014including Elroy Air, Zipline, Joby Aviation, Nuro, and Archer Aviation\u2014with no public comparables available for direct benchmarking.\n\nValuation analysis relies on a single applicable method: stage-progression analysis. Using total capital raised ($40M) as a proxy for post-money valuation at Series A close, application of a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical for Series B advancement yields an implied valuation of $76M. This reflects the expectation of equity value accretion between Series A and Series B financing rounds within the sector.\n\nA formal peer-median approach is not applicable here. While five same-sector peers exist, only one falls within the narrow same-stage filtering criteria; adjacent-stage and similar-valuation-tier filters yielded insufficient data. Relying on all-sector medians would introduce material noise given the heterogeneity of business models and maturity across the broader Drones & Autonomous landscape.\n\nThe triangulated valuation range of $65M (low) to $87M (high), centered on $76M (median), is supported by stage-progression analysis alone. Key uncertainties include the absence of granular peer-stage and revenue metrics, the scarcity of same-stage comparable transactions, and sector-wide variation in technical risk and capital intensity. Investors should weight this range as preliminary pending access to Asylon's operating metrics and a more densely populated peer set at Series B stage.",
