      "narrative": "Atom Computing is a Series B-stage semiconductor company that has raised $300M+ to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comparable universe of 11 firms spanning chips and semiconductors\u20143 public (ALAB, NVDA, AMD) and 8 private peers including Positron AI, Cerebras, SambaNova Systems, PsiQuantum, and Etched, representing adjacent and same-stage companies.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, anchoring to the $300M total raised as a value proxy and applying a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical for Series B progression, implies a valuation of $570M. Peer-median analysis across 5 same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables\u2014Positron AI ($1.0B, Series B), d-Matrix ($2.0B, Series C), Etched ($5.0B, Series C), SambaNova Systems ($11.0B, Series A), and DEEPX ($529M, Series C)\u2014yields a median valuation of $2.0B, with a range of $529M to $11.0B.\n\nSynthesizing both methods produces a triangulated range of $484M (low) to $2.3B (high), with a median of $1.3B. The wide dispersion reflects significant stage and valuation heterogeneity within the semiconductor frontier-tech cohort. Key uncertainties include the relevance of early-stage outliers like SambaNova ($11.0B at Series A) and the degree to which Atom's specific technology and market position align with later-stage, higher-valued peers rather than stage-matched comparables.",
