      "narrative": "Primer AI is a Series D defense and security company that has raised $237M to date. The valuation analysis draws on two core methods triangulated against a peer set of 4 private same-stage comparables (Helsing, Saronic, Chaos Industries, Onebrief) spanning $2.1B to $18.0B in valuation, plus 2 public defense contractors and 8 additional private peers for directional context.\n\nThe stage-progression method, applying a 1.5x step-up multiplier typical of Series D-to-later advancement, yields $356M. The peer-median approach, based on the four same-sector, same-stage comparables, produces a median of $6.9B, with a range of $2.1B to $18.0B. These methods are materially divergent, reflecting the wide spread in defense-tech valuations at this stage and uncertainty around Primer's relative positioning within the peer cohort.\n\nTriangulation across both methods supports a valuation range of $302M (low), $3.6B (median), and $7.9B (high). The wide band reflects two competing dynamics: the stage-progression floor anchored to capital deployed and the peer-median ceiling set by comparable funding environments in the sector. Key uncertainties include Primer's revenue traction relative to peers, customer concentration and contract visibility, and whether recent defense-tech valuations reflect sustainable fundamentals or mark-to-market inflation. Resolution of these factors will determine positioning within the derived range.",
