      "narrative": "Mara is a pre-seed stage defense and security company founded by Daniel Kofman and Sriram Raghu. The company has raised $1.6M to date. The Defense & Security sector includes 2 public comparables (DRSHF, IDEAFORGE.NS) and 8 private peers, notably Anduril Industries, Helsing, Shield AI, Saronic, and Quantum-Systems.\n\nStage-progression valuation is the applicable method here. Using $300M as a proxy based on total capital raised, and applying a 2.5x multiplier typical of pre-seed to next-stage progression in this sector, the analysis implies a $750M valuation. Peer-median analysis is not applicable due to insufficient same-stage or adjacent-stage comparables within the defense sector\u2014while 21 total defense peers exist, fewer than three meet the narrow filters for stage and valuation tier. Relying on broader sector medians would introduce undue noise.\n\nThe triangulated range is $638M to $862M, with a central estimate of $750M. This range reflects the single applicable method and carries material uncertainty around the appropriate step-up multiplier and the representativeness of the $300M proxy itself. Key risks to valuation include stage-dependent fundraising success, competitive positioning within the crowded defense tech landscape, and regulatory constraints inherent to the sector. A fuller peer set at equivalent stages would strengthen conviction in any valuation conclusion.",
