      "narrative": "Flock Safety, a Series G defense and security technology company, is valued at $7.5B post-money on $1.4B+ total capital raised. The peer universe comprises 10 comparable companies: 2 public (DRSHF, IDEAFORGE.NS) and 8 private-market defense tech firms including Shield AI ($12.7B, Series G), Helsing ($18.0B, Series D), and Saronic ($9.2B, Series D).\n\nTwo valuation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, using a typical 1.25x step-up multiplier from current Series G post-money, yields $9.4B. Peer-median analysis across 9 same-sector comparables with similar valuation tier produced $4.5B, with peer valuations ranging $2.1B to $18.0B. The disparity reflects material variance in stage and scale within the defense tech cohort.\n\nTriangulating these methods produces a valuation range of $3.8B (low) to $10.8B (high), with a median of $6.9B. The current $7.5B valuation sits slightly above the triangulated median, within the upper-middle quartile. Key uncertainties include capital efficiency relative to peer benchmarks, revenue scale relative to funding deployed, and market-specific defensibility within the crowded frontier-defense sector. The wide peer range ($2.1B\u2013$18.0B) reflects limited stage-peer comparability and heightened sensitivity to recent funding and growth trajectory.",
