      "narrative": "Longshot Space is a seed-stage space and aerospace company founded by Mike Grace and Nathan Saichek that has raised $10M+ to date. The valuation universe comprises 5 public comparables (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private peers including SpaceX, Sierra Space, and Planet Labs, though narrow peer matching at seed stage yields limited datapoints for direct comparison.\n\nThe stage-progression method is the primary applicable approach, using the $10M total raised as a valuation proxy and applying a 2.5x step-up multiplier typical of seed-to-next-stage advancement, yielding $25M. The peer-median method cannot be reliably applied: while 11 same-sector private comparables exist, filtering for identical stage, adjacent stage, or similar valuation tier produces fewer than the three minimum datapoints required for statistical robustness. Public-comp anchoring via P/S multiples (sector median 23.9x across 6 tickers) is inapplicable without disclosed revenue figures, which private companies rarely provide.\n\nThe triangulated range is $21M to $29M, centered at $25M. This range reflects the single applicable method with a \u00b115% sensitivity band. Key uncertainties are the absence of same-stage peer comparables for validation and the complete lack of revenue disclosure, which prevents multiple cross-check methodologies. A post-seed financing round or revenue disclosure would materially improve valuation precision.",
