      "narrative": "Medra is a Series A-stage biotech company founded by Michelle Lee that has raised $52M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a reference universe of 3 public peers in Biotech & Health (RXRX, TEM, ONT.L) and 8 private companies operating in the same sector, including Colossal Biosciences, Abridge, and Recursion Pharmaceuticals.\n\nOf the three valuation methods examined, only stage-progression proved applicable. This method uses the $52M total raised as a valuation proxy and applies a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A advancement to the next funding stage, yielding an implied valuation of $104M. The peer-median approach could not be applied due to insufficient narrow-match comparables\u2014while 8 same-sector peers exist, fewer than 3 met Stage A / adjacent-stage / similar-tier filters simultaneously. Public-comp anchoring using the sector's 5.5x median P/S multiple across the three public tickers was inapplicable because Medra's revenue is not on file, a common limitation for private companies.\n\nThe triangulated valuation range is $88M to $120M, with a median of $104M. This analysis relies on a single defensible method and therefore carries material uncertainty. Key risks include the broad step-up multiplier's applicability to Medra's specific risk profile and stage dynamics, and the absence of revenue visibility that would strengthen the analysis. Additional data on comparable Series A biotech exits or Medra's own revenue traction would substantially narrow this range.",
