      "narrative": "Abridge is a Series E biotech and health company founded by Shiv Rao, currently valued at $5.3B post-money following $1.2B+ in cumulative fundraising. The valuation analysis draws from a comparable universe of 10 firms spanning the Biotech & Health sector: 3 public companies (RXRX, TEM, ONT.L) and 7 private peers including Colossal Biosciences, Chai Discovery, New Limit, Recursion Pharmaceuticals, and Freenome.\n\nTwo methods triangulate the valuation. Stage-progression analysis applies a 1.4x step-up multiplier typical of Series E to Series F advancement, yielding $7.4B. Peer-median benchmarking across 5 same-sector comparables with similar valuation tiers produces a median of $3.1B, with a range spanning $1.1B to $10.3B. Public-comp anchoring via Price-to-Sales multiples proved inapplicable due to Abridge's private status and undisclosed revenue figures; the sector median P/S of 5.5x across the three public tickers cannot be applied without target revenue data.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a range of $2.6B to $8.5B, with a median of $5.3B\u2014aligned with Abridge's current valuation. The substantial spread between peer median ($3.1B) and stage-progression ($7.4B) reflects sensitivity to both comparable selection and growth rate assumptions. Key uncertainties include Abridge's revenue trajectory, the representativeness of early-stage biotech peers at later funding stages, and public market comparables trading at compressed multiples relative to private valuations.",
