      "narrative": "PsiQuantum is a private-stage semiconductor company founded by Jeremy O'Brien, Terry Rudolph, Peter Shadbolt, and Mark Thompson, currently valued at $7B after raising $1B in total capital. The valuation assessment draws on a peer set of 11 comparable companies across chips and semiconductors\u20143 public (ALAB, NVDA, AMD) and 8 private entities including SambaNova Systems, Etched, Tenstorrent, Rebellions, and Cerebras.\n\nPeer-median analysis, the primary applicable valuation method, examined 6 same-sector comparables at similar valuation tiers. The peer median across this set is $2.5B, with a range spanning $2.0B to $11.0B. SambaNova Systems trades at the high end ($11.0B, Series A), while Tenstorrent, Rebellions, and public-traded Ouster cluster between $2.3B and $2.7B across Series D and pre-IPO stages.\n\nThe triangulated valuation range is $2.1B to $2.9B (median $2.5B), indicating PsiQuantum's current $7B valuation sits substantially above comparable companies at equivalent or more mature stages. Key uncertainties include differentiation in proprietary quantum chip architecture relative to peers, capital intensity and path to revenue generation, and whether the $7B reflects sector enthusiasm premia not supported by peer trading multiples. With only one valuation method applied, triangulation lacks robustness; additional revenue or market-based metrics would strengthen conviction in any range assessment.",
