      "narrative": "d-Matrix, a Series C semiconductor company founded by Sid Sheth and Sudeep Bhoja, is valued at $2.0B post-money following $450M in total capital raised. The valuation is anchored against a comp universe of 11 private frontier-chip firms and 3 public semiconductor peers (NVDA, AMD, ALAB), including stage-adjacent companies like Etched ($5.0B Series C), Tenstorrent ($2.7B Series D), and DEEPX ($529M Series C).\n\nTwo triangulation methods apply to d-Matrix. Stage-progression analysis, applying a typical 1.7x Series C-to-next-stage multiplier to the $2.0B last post-money, implies a valuation of $3.4B. Peer-median analysis across four same-sector peers at Series B through D stages yields a median valuation of $1.9B, with the peer range spanning $529M to $5.0B. The wide dispersion reflects material stage and product-maturity variance across the sample.\n\nThe triangulated valuation range is $1.6B (low) to $3.9B (high), with a median of $2.6B. The current $2.0B valuation sits slightly below the median, reflecting modest step-up from Series B entry dynamics. Key uncertainties include commercialization timeline, competitive positioning relative to Etched and Tenstorrent, and the duration to cash-flow inflection in a capital-intensive semiconductor development cycle.",
