      "narrative": "FleetZero is a Series A-stage transportation company founded by Steven Henderson and Mike Carter, which has raised $43M to date. The relevant comp universe comprises eight private firms in the Transportation sector, including Rivian, The Boring Company, Einride, Pipedream, and Parallel Systems; no public comparables exist in this space. Given the early-stage nature and nascent competitive landscape, traditional peer-median valuation is not applicable\u2014no same-stage or adjacent-stage peers with sufficient density exist to establish a reliable benchmark.\n\nStage-progression methodology is the primary applicable triangulation method here. Using the $43M total capital raised as a valuation proxy and applying a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical for Series A-to-subsequent-stage progression yields an implied valuation of $86M. This reflects the expected value accretion between funding rounds absent material operational or market deterioration.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $73M to $99M, with a median point estimate of $86M. This single-method approach introduces material uncertainty; validation would benefit from revenue multiples or unit economics if disclosed, and from closer peer traction data as the Transportation frontier-tech space matures. Key sensitivities include burn rate, customer concentration, and technology differentiation relative to the broader competitor set.",
