      "narrative": "Isar Aerospace is a Series C-stage space and aerospace company that has raised $650M+ to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comparable universe of 3 same-sector, same-stage private companies (Sierra Space, Varda Space Industries, Skyryse) and 5 public Space & Aerospace tickers (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) for anchoring context.\n\nTwo quantitative methods prove applicable. The Stage-Progression method applies a typical 1.7x step-up multiplier to the $650M raised proxy, implying a valuation of $1.1B. The Peer-Median method examines three same-stage, same-sector private comparables with valuations ranging from $1.1B to $8.0B, yielding a median of $1.5B. Public-Comp anchoring cannot be applied because the target's revenue is not publicly available. Public Space & Aerospace peers trade at a 23.9x price-to-sales median, but this multiple cannot be operationalized without disclosed revenue figures.\n\nTriangulating the two applicable methods yields a valuation range of $939M (low) to $1.7B (high), with a median of $1.3B. The primary uncertainty is the wide dispersion within the peer set\u2014the $8.0B outlier (Sierra Space) reflects heterogeneity in business model maturity and market positioning within commercial spaceflight. Absence of target revenue limits anchoring to cost-of-capital and stage-based methods. Further diligence on revenue trajectory and unit economics would refine the range.",
