      "narrative": "Latitude is a Series B-stage space & aerospace company that has raised \u20ac50M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a peer set of five same-sector, same/adjacent-stage private companies: Sierra Space ($8.0B Series C), Cowboy Space Corporation ($2.0B Series B), Varda Space Industries ($1.5B Series C), Aalyria ($1.3B Series B), and Skyryse ($1.1B Series C).\n\nThe peer-median method is the applicable triangulation approach. The five comparable companies span a valuation range of $1.1B to $8.0B, with a median of $1.5B. This method directly anchors the analysis given alignment on sector and development stage. A public-comp anchoring approach using the 6-ticker Space & Aerospace universe (median P/S of 23.9x) cannot be applied, as Latitude's revenue is not disclosed\u2014a common constraint in private company valuation.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $1.3B to $1.7B, centered on $1.5B. This median reflects the peer cohort but carries meaningful uncertainty given the wide dispersion in the comp set ($1.1B to $8.0B). Stage heterogeneity within the peer group\u2014with two Series C valuations in the sample\u2014introduces additional variance. Validation would benefit from revenue or funding-round pricing data if available.",
