      "narrative": "ICEYE is a Series E-stage space & aerospace company founded by Rafa\u0142 Modrzewski and Pekka Laurila, currently valued at \u20ac10.5B (~$12B) after raising $730M+. The target operates within a fragmented peer universe of 11 private Space & Aerospace companies and 5 public comparables (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL).\n\nValuation triangulation is constrained by limited methodological applicability. Stage-progression analysis, applying a 1.4x multiplier typical of Series E advancement to the $730M total raised proxy, yields $1.0B. Peer-median analysis is not applicable: while 11 same-sector private peers exist, insufficient datapoints meet narrow filtering criteria (same-stage or adjacent-stage at comparable valuation tiers), rendering such benchmarking unreliable. Public-comp anchoring, though technically feasible using the Space & Aerospace median P/S of 23.9x across five tickers, cannot be executed because ICEYE's revenue is not disclosed\u2014a common constraint for private company valuation.\n\nThe single applicable method supports a narrow range of $869M to $1.2B, centered at $1.0B. This analysis reveals a substantial gap between the stage-progression-derived range and the company's stated valuation of ~$12B. Key uncertainties include the absence of comparable transaction data at ICEYE's scale, unavailable revenue metrics needed for public-comp calibration, and the structural illiquidity of Series E equity that typically commands limited discount to stated valuations in absence of external validation.",
