      "narrative": "IQM Quantum Computers is a public-stage quantum computing company that has raised \u20ac600M+ to date. Valuation analysis relies on peer comparison within the quantum computing sector, which includes 3 public peers (IonQ, Rigetti Computing, D-Wave Quantum) and 8 private comparables. The peer universe spans market capitalizations from $1.9B to $13.0B.\n\nA peer-median approach using 4 same-sector, same-stage comparables (IonQ at $13.0B, D-Wave Quantum at $6.3B, Rigetti Computing at $4.5B, and Infleqtion at $1.9B) yields a median valuation of $5.4B. This represents the central point in a peer range spanning from $1.9B at the low end to $13.0B at the high end. The wide dispersion reflects heterogeneity in quantum architectures, commercialization progress, and market positioning across the cohort.\n\nThe triangulated valuation range supported by this analysis is $4.6B to $6.2B, centered on the $5.4B peer median. Key uncertainties include the limited methodological basis (single approach), the extreme outlier valuation of IonQ relative to other peers, and the nascent stage of quantum computing commercialization, which limits the predictive power of current peer multiples. Additional methods incorporating revenue multiples, discounted cash flow, or stage-adjusted capital efficiency would be required to strengthen conviction in this range.",
