      "narrative": "ANYbotics is a Series B robotics and manufacturing company that has raised $50M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comparison universe of 9 private peers and 1 public comparable, all operating in the robotics and manufacturing sector. Key private comparables include Bedrock Robotics, Dexterity, Divergent, Exotec, and Locus Robotics, representing a robust dataset of same-sector, same/adjacent-stage companies.\n\nTwo valuation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis applies a 1.9x multiplier to the $50M raised, implying $95M valuation based on typical Series B step-up dynamics. Peer-median analysis across four direct comparables\u2014Bedrock Robotics ($1.8B), Dexterity ($1.6B), Hadrian ($1.6B), and Nimble Robotics ($1.0B)\u2014yields a median valuation of $1.6B, with a range spanning $1.0B to $1.8B.\n\nThe triangulated analysis produces a low estimate of $81M, a median of $860M, and a high of $1.9B. The wide dispersion reflects material tension between capital-efficiency metrics (stage-progression) and peer trading multiples in an active, well-capitalized subsector. The median estimate of $860M sits between the two methods, though significant uncertainty persists around whether ANYbotics' specific technology maturity, customer traction, and market position align with the peer median or reflect a discount. Resolution requires granular assessment of product-market fit, competitive positioning, and gross margins relative to the peer set.",
