      "narrative": "Xtend, a Series B defense and security company founded by Aviv Shapira, has raised $100M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a peer set of 10 comparable companies spanning the Defense & Security sector\u20142 public (DRSHF, IDEAFORGE.NS) and 8 private firms including Dream Security, Harmattan AI, Code Metal, Castelion, and Defense Unicorns.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. The stage-progression method uses the $944M total-raised proxy as a base and applies a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical of Series B advancement, yielding $1.8B. The peer-median method anchors to a cohort of 7 same-sector, same-stage comparables with a median valuation of $1.0B (range: $300M\u2013$3.0B), reflecting the dispersion observed in the Defense & Security space at this stage. This method directly reflects observable market pricing of peers at Xtend's development and funding stage.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $850M (low) to $2.1B (high), with a median point of $1.4B. The stage-progression and peer-median approaches converge on a midpoint near $1.4B, though material spread persists across the range. Key uncertainties include customer concentration and revenue predictability in the defense contracting environment, execution risk at Series B scale, and the relative weighting of outlier peers (Dream Security at $3.0B) versus the tighter cluster around $1.0B\u2013$1.4B.",
