      "narrative": "Percepto is a Series C autonomous drone company founded by Dor Abuhasira, Ariel Avitan, Sagi Blonder, and Raviv Raz. The broader Drones & Autonomous sector includes six private peers (Zipline, Joby Aviation, Nuro, Archer Aviation, Elroy Air, and others) and no public comparables, creating a constrained comp universe for direct market-based validation.\n\nThe valuation analysis applied one primary methodology: stage-progression analysis using total capital raised ($128M) as a proxy for current enterprise value, then applying a 1.7x multiplier typical of Series C-to-subsequent-round step-ups. This produced an implied valuation of $218M. A peer-median approach was not applicable due to insufficient granular peer data\u2014while five same-sector companies exist, none met the filters for same-stage or adjacent-stage comparables with similar valuation tiers, making sector-wide medians unreliable for this company's profile.\n\nThe single-method triangulation yields a median valuation of $218M, with a range of $185M (low) to $250M (high) derived from sensitivity around the 1.7x multiplier. The range reflects stage-typical expansion assumptions but carries material uncertainty given the absence of direct peer validation and early-stage market dynamics in autonomous systems. Key risks include the nascent state of drone commercialization, regulatory variability, and limited public market comps for capital structure benchmarking. Further clarity on Percepto's revenue run-rate and customer concentration would refine this estimate.",
