      "narrative": "Mujin is a Series C robotics and manufacturing automation company that has raised $85M+ to date. The valuation analysis draws on a peer universe of 9 comparable companies\u20141 public and 8 private\u2014spanning the same sector and stage. Key private peers include Hadrian, Nimble Robotics, and Exotec, with valuations ranging from $1.0B to $2.0B at Series B through Series D.\n\nTwo methods were applied to triangulate fair value. The Stage-Progression method, which applies a 1.7x multiplier to total capital raised as a proxy for current enterprise value, yields $144M. The Peer-Median method benchmarks Mujin against five same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables (Exotec, Bedrock Robotics, Dexterity, Hadrian, and Nimble Robotics), producing a median valuation of $1.6B with a range of $1.0B\u2013$2.0B. The divergence reflects stage maturity differences within the peer set: Series B and Series D peers command higher multiples than Series C.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $123M (low) to $1.9B (high), with a median of $897M. The wide range reflects material uncertainty around Mujin's relative technology maturity, revenue scale, and market penetration versus peers. Stage-progression suggests a conservative floor, while peer comparables anchor the upper bound. Resolution of execution risk and competitive positioning will likely narrow this range substantially at Series D.",
