      "narrative": "Pixxel is a Series B space and aerospace company that has raised $95M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a peer set of five same-sector, same/adjacent-stage private companies (Sierra Space, Cowboy Space Corporation, Varda Space Industries, Aalyria, and Skyryse) and six public comparables (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL, and one additional ticker).\n\nTwo valuation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis, using total raised as a proxy for current valuation and applying a typical 1.9x step-up multiplier from Series B onward, implies a valuation of $180M. Peer-median analysis across the five private comparables yields a median valuation of $1.5B, with a range spanning $1.1B to $8.0B. Public-comp anchoring cannot be applied because Pixxel's revenue is not on file. The peer median of 23.9x price-to-sales across public Space & Aerospace names provides directional context but cannot be operationalized without the target's revenue figure.\n\nThe triangulated valuation range is $153M (low) to $1.7B (high), with a median of $840M. The wide spread reflects material dispersion within the peer set, particularly the $8.0B valuation of Sierra Space at the upper end. Key uncertainties include Pixxel's revenue trajectory, the stage heterogeneity within comparables (mix of Series B and Series C), and whether public multiples will compress or expand. A valuation in the $800M\u2013$1.2B range appears most defensible against the peer median, though stage-progression alone suggests meaningful upside remains to next-round valuation expectations.",
