      "narrative": "Tenstorrent, a Series D-stage semiconductor design company, was last valued at $2.7B post-money after raising $1B+. The relevant comp universe spans 11 private frontier-chip firms (Cerebras, SambaNova Systems, Etched, Rebellions, and others) and 3 public semiconductor peers (ALAB, NVDA, AMD), all operating in the Chips & Semiconductors sector.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression assumes a typical 1.5x step-up from Series D to the next funding round, implying $4.0B. Peer-median analysis across three same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables\u2014Etched ($5.0B), d-Matrix ($2.0B), and DEEPX ($529M)\u2014yields a median of $2.0B, with a range spanning $529M to $5.0B. These methods anchor to Tenstorrent's last posted valuation and market precedent.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $1.7B (low) to $4.7B (high), with a median of $3.0B. The current $2.7B valuation sits within this range, slightly below the median. Key uncertainties include the dispersion across peer valuations\u2014a 9.5x spread from min to max\u2014and stage-progression variability, which depends on execution metrics and market conditions at the next funding event. The analysis rests on limited peer count (3 comps for median) and heterogeneity in chip-company business models and funding timelines.",
      "lastUpdated": "2026-08-02T11:00:32+00:00"
