      "narrative": "Solinftec, a Series B robotics and manufacturing company that has raised $40M to date, is valued through triangulation against a comparable universe of 9 private peers and 1 public company in the sector. Primary comparables include Bedrock Robotics ($1.8B Series B), Dexterity ($1.6B Series B), Hadrian ($1.6B Series C), and Nimble Robotics ($1.0B Series C).\n\nTwo valuation methods were applied. The stage-progression approach, using the $40M raised as a proxy for current valuation and applying a 1.9x multiplier typical of Series B progression, implies $76M. The peer-median method anchors to the median valuation of the four comparable companies at $1.6B, reflecting the range from $1.0B to $1.8B observed in the peer set. This substantial divergence reflects the early-stage nature of Solinftec relative to more mature Series C peers and the wide dispersion in robotics sector valuations.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $65M (low) to $1.9B (high), with a median of $850M. The wide range reflects genuine uncertainty around Solinftec's technology maturity, market traction, and capital efficiency relative to established peers. The peer-median result carries greater weight given it is based on direct market comparables; however, the stage-progression method suggests potential for substantial upside if the company demonstrates execution in line with its peer cohort.",
