      "narrative": "Neura Robotics, a Series B robotics and manufacturing company founded by David Reger, is evaluated against a comp universe of 9 private and 1 public peer\u2014a mix spanning comparable and adjacent stages within the sector. The target has raised $123.3M to date.\n\nTwo valuation methods were applied. The Stage-Progression approach, anchoring to the $1.4B total-raised proxy and applying a 1.9x Series B step-up multiplier, implies a valuation of $2.7B. The Peer-Median method benchmarks against four same-sector peers (Bedrock Robotics at $1.8B, Dexterity at $1.6B, Hadrian at $1.6B, and Nimble Robotics at $1.0B), yielding a median of $1.6B and a range of $1.0B to $1.8B. These two methods reflect different weighting: stage-based momentum versus current market-observed valuations for comparable-stage companies.\n\nTriangulation across both methods supports a range of $1.4B to $3.1B, with a median of $2.1B. The $1.1B spread between the peer-median and stage-progression methods reflects material uncertainty around whether Neura's trajectory and market conditions align with peer valuations or steeper stage-advance premiums. Key drivers of ultimate valuation include execution on proprietary capabilities and capital efficiency relative to the peer cohort.",
