      "narrative": "Dronamics, a Series A autonomous delivery drone platform founded by Svilen and Konstantin Rangelov, is evaluated within a competitive landscape of eight private companies in the Drones & Autonomous sector. The comp universe includes well-capitalized peers such as Zipline, Joby Aviation, Nuro, Archer Aviation, and Elroy Air, though no public comparables exist in the narrowly defined segment. The absence of public market data and limited same-stage peer disclosure constrain traditional valuation approaches.\n\nGiven Dronamics' $43.2M in total capital raised to date, the Stage-Progression method is the primary applicable approach. This method applies a standard 2.0x multiplier typical of Series A advancement to subsequent funding rounds, yielding an implied valuation of $86M. A peer-median approach was not viable; while five peers operate in the Drones & Autonomous space, none satisfy the narrow filters of identical stage, adjacent-stage proximity, or comparable valuation tier, preventing statistically meaningful median extraction.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $73M (low) to $99M (high), with a median point estimate of $86M. This range reflects the upside embedded in typical Series A progression mechanics applied to the company's demonstrated capital deployment. Key uncertainties include the absence of comparable transaction multiples at identical stage maturity, limited public market reference points for autonomous vehicle platform valuations, and sector-specific execution risk that peer comparables do not yet price. Further refinement would require disclosed financial metrics or revenue traction.",
