      "narrative": "Grain Weevil is a seed-stage robotics and manufacturing company founded by Chad and Ben Johnson that has raised $3.5M to date. The valuation universe comprises eight private robotics and manufacturing firms, including peers such as Walden Robotics, Divergent, Exotec, Locus Robotics, and Bedrock Robotics, alongside one public comparable (ticker 277810.KQ).\n\nThe Stage-Progression method is applicable and forms the primary valuation vector. Using total capital raised ($3.5M) as a baseline proxy and applying a typical 2.5x multiplier for progression from Seed to the next financing stage yields an implied valuation of $9M. The Peer-Median method is not applicable due to insufficient data density: while eight same-sector peers exist in the broader Robotics & Manufacturing universe, filtering for same-stage, adjacent-stage, or similar-valuation-tier comparables yielded fewer than three datapoints, rendering sector-wide medians unreliably broad.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $7M (low) to $10M (high), with a median point of $9M. This range reflects the single applicable method and carries material uncertainty stemming from limited peer comparability at the seed stage and the absence of narrowly-filtered comparable transaction data. Key sensitivities include the propriety of the 2.5x step-up multiplier for this company's specific risk profile and market conditions, as well as the stage at which the next financing round is expected.",
