      "narrative": "Chef Robotics, a Series A robotics and manufacturing company founded by Rajat Bhageria, has raised $65.6M to date. Valuation analysis relies on two primary methods triangulated against a comp universe of 9 private peers and 1 public comparable (277810.KQ), including Bedrock Robotics, Dexterity, and Walden Robotics.\n\nStage-progression methodology applies a 2.0x step-up multiplier to the $66M raised proxy, implying a $131M valuation. Peer-median analysis across three same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables yields a $1.6B implied valuation, with the peer set ranging from $1.1B (Walden Robotics, Seed stage) to $1.8B (Bedrock Robotics, Series B). The disparate results reflect material differences in peer stage positioning and valuation trajectories within the robotics sector.\n\nTriangulation across both methods supports a valuation range of $112M to $1.9B, with a median of $891M. The wide range reflects key uncertainties: stage alignment among peers (Chef Robotics occupies an intermediate position relative to seed and Series B comparables), pace of revenue or unit growth, and sector-specific risk factors. The peer-median method likely anchors valuation more robustly given the three-firm sample, though the stage-progression approach provides a conservative floor. Resolution of these uncertainties through near-term operational milestones would materially narrow the range.",
