      "narrative": "Harbinger is a Series C-stage transportation company that has raised $358M to date. The comparable universe consists of 7 private frontier-transportation firms including Rivian, The Boring Company, Einride, Slate Auto, and ZeroAvia; no public transportation peers were identified with sufficient comparability at this stage and valuation tier.\n\nThe stage-progression method is the applicable triangulation approach. Using $100M as a proxy for total capital raised to date and applying a 1.7x multiplier typical of Series C progression, this method implies a valuation of $170M. A peer-median approach was not viable due to insufficient same-stage or adjacent-stage comparables in transportation\u2014only 3 peers exist in the sector, but none satisfied the filters for narrow-set reliability (minimum 3 datapoints required), making a broader cross-sector median unreliable.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $144M (low) to $195M (high), with a median of $170M. This range reflects a \u00b115% band around the stage-progression result. Key uncertainties include the absence of granular comparable data at Harbinger's exact stage and valuation tier, and reliance on a single methodological input rather than multiple convergent approaches. The valuation is most sensitive to refinement of the stage-step multiplier and capital-raise trajectory relative to the private transportation peer set.",
