      "narrative": "Lumafield is a Series C robotics and manufacturing company that has raised $142M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comp universe of nine private robotics firms at Series B through Series D stages, plus one public comparable, reflecting the early-stage nature of the sector.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. The stage-progression method, using $10M as a proxy for total capital deployed, applies a 1.7x multiplier typical of Series C advancement, yielding $17M. The peer-median method examines five same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables\u2014Exotec ($2.0B, Series D), Bedrock Robotics ($1.8B, Series B), Dexterity ($1.6B, Series B), Hadrian ($1.6B, Series C), and Nimble Robotics ($1.0B, Series C)\u2014producing a median valuation of $1.6B with a range from $1.0B to $2.0B.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $14M to $1.9B, with a median of $834M. The wide dispersion reflects material uncertainty in comparable selection and stage-appropriate value creation. The peer-median method carries greater weight given Lumafield's Series C positioning and the availability of same-stage comparables; however, the $1.6B median must be treated as a ceiling pending validation of revenue growth, unit economics, and competitive positioning relative to the identified peer set. Key uncertainties include customer concentration, manufacturing scalability, and differentiation within an increasingly dense robotics market.",
