      "narrative": "Modern Intelligence is a Seed-stage defense and security company founded by John Dulin, Joe Cieslik, and Tristan Tager, having raised $5.12M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a comparable universe of 10 companies\u20142 public (DRSHF, IDEAFORGE.NS) and 8 private peers including UFORCE, Anduril Industries, Helsing, Shield AI, and Saronic\u2014spanning the same sector at Seed and Series A stages.\n\nTwo valuation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis uses the $5.12M raised as a proxy base value and applies a 2.5x multiplier typical for Seed-to-next-stage advancement, implying a $13M valuation. Peer-median analysis draws from three same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables: UFORCE ($1.0B, Seed), Singularity ($400M, Series A), and NODA AI ($125M, Series A). The median of these three peers is $400M, with a range spanning $125M to $1.0B.\n\nThe triangulated analysis across both methods supports a valuation range of $11M to $460M, with a median of $206M. The wide dispersion reflects material uncertainty around (1) the appropriate peer weighting given the significant valuation heterogeneity within early-stage defense tech, and (2) Modern Intelligence's positioning relative to outliers like UFORCE. Stage-progression yields only a lower bound; peer multiples dominate the range. Refinement would require clarity on product differentiation and go-to-market traction relative to named comparables.",
