      "narrative": "Swift Beat, a Series A defense and security company founded by Eric Schmidt, is evaluated against a peer universe of 10 same-sector companies at comparable or adjacent stages\u2014comprising 2 public equities and 8 private firms including Anduril Industries, Helsing, and Shield AI.\n\nTwo valuation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, anchoring to the company's $50M total raised and applying a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A advancement, implies a $100M valuation. Peer-median analysis across the 10-company defense and security comparison set yields a $1.0B median valuation, with a range spanning $125M to $3.0B. The peer sample includes Dream Security at $3.0B (Series B), Harmattan AI at $1.4B (Series B), Code Metal at $1.2B (Series B), and Castelion and Defense Unicorns both at $1.0B (Series B).\n\nTriangulation of both methods supports a valuation range of $85M to $1.1B, with a median of $550M. The wide dispersion reflects material uncertainty: peer comps cluster primarily at Series B, one stage ahead, and the sector exhibits pronounced valuation heterogeneity. Swift Beat's position within this range depends on revenue trajectory, customer concentration, and technology defensibility relative to the peer cohort. Additional data on revenue multiples or customer acquisition costs would sharpen the estimate toward the lower or upper bounds.",
