      "narrative": "ClearSpace, a Series A+ stage company in Space & Aerospace founded by Luc Piguet and Muriel Richard, has raised $36M to date. The valuation landscape includes 5 public comparables (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private peers spanning the sector, with top-tier private comparables including SpaceX, Sierra Space, and Planet Labs.\n\nStandard triangulation methods encounter material constraints. A peer-median approach is inapplicable: while 11 same-sector peers exist in Space & Aerospace, filtering by stage, adjacency, or valuation tier yields fewer than the minimum 3 datapoints required for statistical reliability. Public-comp anchoring cannot be executed because ClearSpace's revenue is not disclosed\u2014a common limitation for private companies\u2014and applying the sector P/S median of 23.9x across 6 public tickers without a revenue figure would be meaningless.\n\nThe absence of sufficient narrow-set comparables and missing revenue data prevents quantitative triangulation at this stage. Further analysis would require either (1) revenue disclosure from the target, (2) identification of at least three Series A+ or adjacent-stage Space & Aerospace peers with disclosed valuations, or (3) transaction multiples from recent financings in the subsector. Until these inputs materialize, a valuation range cannot be defensibly derived from the available data.",
