      "narrative": "Archer Materials is a publicly listed quantum computing company currently valued at A$59.9M (~US$39M), having raised $25M+ to date. The quantum computing sector comprises a mixed cohort of 11 comparable companies\u20143 public and 8 private\u2014including peers such as IonQ, D-Wave Quantum, Rigetti Computing, and Infleqtion across similar development stages.\n\nValuation analysis applied peer-median triangulation against four same-sector, same-stage public comparables. The median valuation across this peer set stands at $5.4B, with a range spanning $1.9B (Infleqtion) to $13.0B (IonQ). This dispersion reflects material variance in technology maturity, capital efficiency, and commercialization progress within the quantum computing landscape. The peer-median method represents the primary applicable triangulation approach given the limited size of directly comparable public firms.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $4.6B to $6.2B, centered on the peer median of $5.4B. This implies a substantial uplift from Archer's current market capitalization of $39M. Key uncertainties include the durability of peer valuations in an early-stage sector with limited revenue visibility, the relevance of public company multiples to a capital-efficient pre-revenue or early-revenue stage entity, and differentiation in technical roadmap execution relative to the broader peer cohort. The wide spread among established peers ($1.9B\u2013$13.0B) underscores material dispersion in market pricing for quantum computing approaches.",
