      "narrative": "Nox Metals is a Seed-stage robotics and manufacturing company founded by Zane Hengsperger that has raised $5.1M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comp universe of 9 private peers in robotics and manufacturing alongside 1 public comparable, though narrow peer availability constrains the analytical approach.\n\nStage-progression methodology is the primary applicable technique here. Using total raised ($5.1M) as a valuation proxy and applying a 2.5x multiplier typical of Seed-to-next-stage progression yields an implied valuation of $13M. This method is appropriate given the early stage and limited peer overlap; however, a traditional peer-median approach could not be applied due to insufficient same-stage or adjacent-stage comparables within the robotics and manufacturing sector. While 8 private peers exist in the broader sector\u2014including Walden Robotics, Divergent, Exotec, Locus Robotics, and Bedrock Robotics\u2014none satisfied the criteria for narrow peer clustering.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $11M (low) to $15M (high), with $13M as the median estimate. This range reflects stage-typical progression rather than market multiples. Key uncertainties include the lack of direct peer validation, which limits confidence in the step-up multiplier selection, and the absence of revenue or unit economics data to ground the valuation in operational performance. A subsequent funding round would provide market-based validation of this range.",
