      "narrative": "Artimus Robotics is a seed-stage robotics and manufacturing company founded by Eric Acome, Shane Mitchell, Nick Kellaris, and Christoph Keplinger. The company has raised $5M to date. The valuation exercise draws on a comp universe of 8 private robotics firms (Walden Robotics, Divergent, Exotec, Locus Robotics, and Bedrock Robotics among them) and 1 public comparable.\n\nThe stage-progression method is applicable and forms the primary valuation anchor. Using the $5M total raised as a proxy for current value and applying a standard 2.5x step-up multiplier typical for progression from seed to next stage yields $12M. Peer-median triangulation is not applicable; while 8 same-sector peers exist, insufficient datapoints cluster at the same stage or adjacent stage to produce a meaningful median\u2014the narrow-filter peer set yielded fewer than three comps, making sector-wide medians unreliable for this analysis.\n\nThe triangulated range spans $11M (low) to $14M (high), with a median of $12M. This range rests on a single method and therefore carries material sensitivity to stage-progression timing assumptions and to the appropriateness of the 2.5x multiplier for this company's specific risk and growth profile. Key uncertainties include the timing and terms of the next funding event and whether this stage-typical multiplier reflects Artimus's technical maturity and market position within the broader robotics sector.",
