      "narrative": "Seurat Technologies, a Series C robotics and manufacturing company that has raised $178M+, is assessed against a comp universe of 9 private companies and 1 public entity operating in the same sector and stage band. The peer set includes Hadrian and Nimble Robotics at Series C, alongside later-stage Exotec ($2.0B, Series D) and earlier-stage Bedrock Robotics ($1.8B, Series B).\n\nTwo valuation methods anchor this analysis. Stage-progression, applying a 1.7x multiplier to the $178M total raised proxy, implies $303M valuation. Peer-median triangulation across five same-sector comparables\u2014Exotec, Bedrock Robotics, Dexterity, Hadrian, and Nimble Robotics\u2014yields a median valuation of $1.6B, with a range spanning $1.0B to $2.0B. These methods produce materially different signals, reflecting variance in how peers have been valued at overlapping stages.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a range of $257M (low) to $1.9B (high), with a median of $976M. The wide dispersion reflects stage heterogeneity within the peer set and uncertainty around Seurat's relative progress toward Series D. Key sensitivities include revenue growth trajectory, capital efficiency relative to peers, and whether comparables at Series B and D prove directionally appropriate for a mid-stage company. Resolution of these factors will be material to narrowing the valuation band.",
