      "narrative": "VulcanForms is a late-stage robotics and manufacturing company founded by John Hart and Martin Feldmann that has raised $575M+. The valuation universe consists of 1 public comparable (ticker 277810.KQ) and 8 private peers in robotics and manufacturing, including Divergent, Exotec, Locus Robotics, Bedrock Robotics, and Dexterity.\n\nThe Stage-Progression method is the sole applicable triangulation approach. Using total capital raised of $575M as a baseline value proxy and applying a 1.2x step-up multiplier typical of late-stage progression yields an implied valuation of $690M. The Peer-Median method cannot be reliably applied due to insufficient narrow peer data; while 8 same-sector comparables exist, filtering by stage, adjacency, or valuation tier produced fewer than the minimum 3 datapoints needed for statistical validity.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $586M to $793M, with a median estimate of $690M. This range reflects the upper and lower bounds of the stage-progression methodology but carries meaningful uncertainty. The primary constraint is reliance on a single method; a more robust triangulation would require either expanded peer comparability data or additional valuation anchors such as revenue multiples or DCF outputs. Given the data available, the $690M median represents the most defensible point estimate, though investors should recognize this reflects capital-raise progression rather than market-based peer validation.",
