      "narrative": "Occam is a Seed-stage biotech company founded by Ana Montero Horas and Andre Marques-Smith that has raised $14M to date. The valuation universe consists of 3 public comparables (RXRX, TEM, ONT.L) and 8 private peers in Biotech & Health, including Colossal Biosciences, Abridge, and Chai Discovery.\n\nStage-progression analysis is the applicable triangulation method given data constraints. Using total capital raised ($14M) as a value proxy and applying a typical Seed-to-next-stage step-up multiplier of 2.5x yields an implied valuation of $35M. Peer-median analysis cannot be applied: while 8 same-sector private peers exist, none satisfy narrow filters for same-stage or adjacent-stage comparables with sufficient sample size. Public-comp anchoring using the Biotech & Health median P/S multiple of 5.5x is also inapplicable due to absence of revenue data on file for this private company.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $30M (low) to $40M (high), with a median point of $35M. This range reflects a single methodological pillar and carries material uncertainty. Key limitations include reliance on a single step-up multiplier without revenue validation, absence of tight peer comparables at Seed stage, and lack of disclosed financial metrics that would enable revenue or earnings multiple anchoring. Additional data on ARR or burn rate would strengthen conviction in this range.",
