      "narrative": "Velaura AI is a Series C-stage semiconductor company founded by Rajiv Khemani, Barun Kar, Saptadeep Pal, and Patrick Xu. The company has raised $343M to date. Valuation analysis draws from a comparable universe of 11 peers across Chips & Semiconductors: 3 public companies (ALAB, NVDA, AMD) and 8 private firms, including same-stage comparables Etched ($5.0B), d-Matrix ($2.0B), and DEEPX ($529M).\n\nTwo triangulation methods apply. Stage-progression analysis applies a typical 1.7x multiplier to the $343M total raised, implying a valuation of $583M. Peer-median analysis uses the three same-sector, same-stage companies, yielding a median valuation of $2.0B, with a range spanning $529M to $5.0B. The wide peer dispersion reflects heterogeneous outcomes within the semiconductor infrastructure space at this stage.\n\nSynthesizing both methods produces a triangulated range of $496M (low) to $2.3B (high), with a median point of $1.3B. The stage-progression method anchors the lower bound, while peer comparables drive the upper end. Key uncertainties include capital efficiency relative to peers, differentiation within the crowded AI-chip market, and the relevance of the wide peer valuation dispersion to Velaura's specific technology and traction profile.",
