      "narrative": "Horizon Quantum Computing is a public-stage quantum computing company that has raised $131M+ including a $110M PIPE completed in December 2025. The valuation analysis relies on a peer-median approach across four same-sector, same-stage comparables: IonQ ($13.0B), D-Wave Quantum ($6.3B), Rigetti Computing ($4.5B), and Infleqtion ($1.9B). The broader quantum computing public market includes IonQ, Rigetti, and Quantinuum, alongside a deeper private comp universe of eight frontier-tech quantum firms.\n\nThe peer-median method is the sole applicable triangulation approach given available data. The four public quantum computing peers generate a median valuation of $5.4B, with a range spanning $1.9B at the low end (Infleqtion) to $13.0B at the high end (IonQ). This dispersion reflects material variance in business model maturity and market positioning within the nascent quantum sector.\n\nThe triangulated valuation range is $4.6B (low) to $6.2B (high), centered on $5.4B. This range assumes Horizon's competitive positioning aligns with the median peer. Key uncertainties include the durability of quantum hardware differentiation, near-term revenue scaling trajectories, and the sustainability of current public market valuations in this early-stage sector. The reliance on a single method and modest peer set (n=4) argues for treating this range as directional rather than precise.",
