      "narrative": "Sabanto is a Series A robotics and manufacturing company that has raised $20M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a peer set of 3 same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables (Bedrock Robotics at $1.8B Series B, Dexterity at $1.6B Series B, and Walden Robotics at $1.1B Seed), supplemented by a broader robotics universe of 8 private companies and 1 public traded comp.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression methodology, using the $20M total raised as a valuation proxy and applying a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A to next-stage advancement, implies $40M. Peer-median analysis across the 3 same-sector comparables yields a median valuation of $1.6B, with a range spanning $1.1B to $1.8B. The peer-median method carries greater weight given its direct calibration to recent funding rounds in robotics at adjacent stages.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $34M (low) to $1.9B (high), with a median of $845M. The wide spread reflects material uncertainty regarding Sabanto's positioning relative to Series B-stage peers\u2014specifically, whether the company demonstrates Series B-ready metrics (revenue scale, market traction, unit economics) or remains closer to early Series A fundamentals. Resolution of revenue trajectory and competitive differentiation within its robotics subsegment will be critical to narrowing this range.",
