      "narrative": "Aclarity, a Series A climate and energy company founded by Julie Bliss Mullen, has raised $14M to date. The valuation assessment draws on a comparable universe of 9 private firms in the climate and energy sector, including peers such as Helion, Redwood Materials, QuantumScape, KoBold Metals, and Electric Hydrogen, alongside one public comparable (LNZA).\n\nThe Stage-Progression method is applicable here, using total capital raised as a proxy for post-money valuation and applying a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A advancement to Series B. This approach yields an implied valuation of $28M. The Peer-Median method could not be reliably applied due to insufficient narrow-set comparables at the same stage, adjacent stage, or similar valuation tier within the climate and energy sector; while nine same-sector peers exist, fewer than three met the filtering criteria needed for statistical confidence.\n\nBased on the Stage-Progression methodology alone, the analysis supports a valuation range of $24M (low) to $32M (high), with a median of $28M. The primary uncertainty stems from limited comparable transactions at Aclarity's stage and valuation tier within the sector. Investors should note that this single-method triangulation carries higher sensitivity to stage-transition assumptions than multi-method approaches would provide. Additional comparable data or transaction precedents would narrow this band.",
