      "narrative": "Akash Systems is a Series B-stage space & aerospace company that has raised $40M+ to date. The valuation analysis triangulates across a comp universe of 5 public equities (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private peers, with particular relevance to same-stage companies including Cowboy Space Corporation ($2.0B, Series B) and Aalyria ($1.3B, Series B).\n\nTwo methods apply quantitatively. Stage-progression analysis uses the $40M total raised as a proxy base value and applies a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical for Series B advancement, yielding $76M. Peer-median valuation benchmarks against five same-sector, same/adjacent-stage companies with a median valuation of $1.5B and a range of $1.1B to $8.0B. Public-comp anchoring was not applicable due to absence of target revenue disclosure, which is standard for private companies. The peer median of $1.5B reflects meaningful dispersion: Sierra Space reaches $8.0B at Series C, while Skyryse sits at $1.1B, also at Series C.\n\nThe triangulated range is $65M (low), $788M (median), and $1.7B (high). The wide band reflects fundamental uncertainty: early-stage revenue or customer concentration data would materially tighten valuation, as would clarity on capital efficiency and near-term path to Series C. The peer-median method dominates the analysis given stage-comparable reference points, though the gap between stage-progression and peer metrics signals that either Akash's capital deployment efficiency differs from peers or market conditions have shifted considerably.",
