      "narrative": "Strider Technologies is a Series C-stage defense and security company that has raised $117M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a peer universe of 12 same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparable companies, comprising 2 public entities and 10 private firms. Leading private comparables include Quantum-Systems ($8.0B, Series C), Helsing ($18.0B, Series D), Saronic ($9.2B, Series D), Chaos Industries ($4.5B, Series D), and Dream Security ($3.0B, Series B). The peer cohort ranges from $300M to $18.0B in valuation.\n\nTwo valuation methods were triangulated. Stage-progression analysis, applying a 1.7x step-up multiplier typical for Series C to next-stage advancement to the $117M total raised baseline, implies $199M. Peer-median analysis across the 12-company comparable set yields $1.8B, reflecting substantial valuation dispersion within the defense and security frontier-tech sector.\n\nThe triangulated range spans $169M (low) to $2.0B (high), with a median implied valuation of $987M. The material gap between stage-progression and peer-median methodologies reflects wide variance in peer-company maturity, capital efficiency, and market positioning. Key uncertainties include Strider's relative revenue scale versus comparables, customer concentration, and near-term path to Series D funding, each of which would materially influence placement within the derived range.",
