      "narrative": "Mythic is a Series D semiconductor company founded by Mike Henry and Dave Fick that has raised $125M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a peer set of 4 same-sector, same/adjacent-stage private companies (Etched, Tenstorrent, d-Matrix, DEEPX) alongside public chip designers (NVDA, AMD, ALAB), supplemented by 8 additional private comparables including Cerebras and SambaNova Systems.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, using $125M total raised as a proxy for current value and applying a 1.5x step-up multiplier typical of Series D advancement, implies a valuation of $188M. Peer-median analysis across the 4 closest comparables yields $2.4B, anchored by Tenstorrent at $2.7B (Series D) and bounded by DEEPX at $529M and Etched at $5.0B. The dispersion reflects heterogeneity in architectural approach and market positioning within the sector.\n\nThese methods triangulate to a range of $159M (low) to $2.7B (high), with a median of $1.3B. The wide spread reflects material uncertainty around Mythic's competitive differentiation relative to better-funded peers like Tenstorrent and Etched. Key variables informing placement within this range include product maturity, customer traction, and addressable market penetration relative to the peer set. Additional diligence on customer pipeline and engineering burn rate would sharpen this estimate.",
