      "narrative": "1X Technologies is a Series B robotics and manufacturing company that has raised $123.5M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comparison universe of nine private robotics firms and one public comparable (ticker 277810.KQ), including same-stage peers Bedrock Robotics ($1.8B), Dexterity ($1.6B), and adjacent-stage peers Hadrian and Nimble Robotics ($1.6B and $1.0B respectively).\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. The stage-progression approach, using total capital raised as a proxy for base value, implies a $3.0B starting valuation stepped up by the typical Series B multiplier of 1.9x, yielding $5.7B. The peer-median method anchors to four same-sector comparables spanning Series B and C stages, producing a median implied valuation of $1.6B with a range of $1.0B to $1.8B. The peer-median approach reflects more conservative, market-tested transaction data, while stage-progression may overweight capital efficiency assumptions.\n\nThe triangulated valuation range spans $1.4B (low) to $6.6B (high), with a median of $3.7B. The substantial spread reflects methodological divergence: peer multiples suggest tighter clustering in the $1.6B to $1.8B band, while stage-progression implies material upside. Key uncertainties include the applicability of stage multipliers in an unproven robotics market and whether 1X's capital intensity and burn profile align with peer benchmarks. A Series B round would likely settle in the $2.5B to $4.5B range absent material technical or market validation.",
