      "narrative": "Orbit Fab, a Series A space and aerospace company founded by Daniel Faber and Jeremy Schiel, has raised $28.5M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a peer universe of 5 public comparables (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private peers including SpaceX, Sierra Space, and Planet Labs, though direct same-stage peers in this subsector remain sparse.\n\nStage-progression analysis, the sole applicable triangulation method, uses the $28.5M raised as a valuation proxy and applies a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A to subsequent-stage transitions, yielding $57M. A peer-median approach was not viable; while 11 same-sector comparables exist, fewer than three fell into relevant stage or valuation-tier bands. Public-comp anchoring via P/S multiples (median 23.9x across the six public Space & Aerospace tickers) could not be applied due to absent revenue disclosure, standard for private companies.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $48M to $66M, with a median point of $57M. This range is bounded by stage-typical progression assumptions rather than market-traded multiples or tight peer clustering. Key uncertainties include the absence of audited financial data, the early-stage nature of the sector itself, and the small denominator of comparable private transactions at this stage. Any refinement would require either revenue disclosure or additional transaction comps in orbital refueling.",
