      "narrative": "Dendra Systems is a Series A climate and energy company that has raised $18M to date. The valuation landscape for frontier-tech climate companies remains sparse; while nine private peers operate in Climate & Energy (including Helion, Redwood Materials, QuantumScape, KoBold Metals, and Electric Hydrogen), none share sufficient overlap in stage and valuation tier to support a robust peer-median approach. One public comparable exists (LNZA). Accordingly, peer triangulation was inapplicable given the absence of three or more narrow-filter matches.\n\nStage-progression methodology is the only applicable valuation tool here. Using total capital raised ($18M) as a baseline proxy and applying a typical Series A to subsequent-stage step-up multiplier of 2.0x yields an implied valuation of $36M. This reflects the financing-round-as-signal framework common when comparable valuations are unavailable.\n\nAnalysis supports a valuation range of $31M (low) to $41M (high), centered on $36M. The median reflects a single methodological input; confidence is therefore contingent on the appropriateness of the 2.0x multiplier for Dendra's specific profile and market conditions. Key uncertainties include the absence of direct peer benchmarks, the stage-progression method's reliance on historical norms that may not apply to frontier climate technology, and whether subsequent-round market conditions have shifted materially from the multiplier's empirical base. Additional data on sector-specific performance metrics would strengthen conviction.",
