      "narrative": "Ultima Genomics is a Series C-stage biotech company that has raised $700M+ under founder Gilad Almogy. Valuation analysis draws on a peer universe of 3 public comparables (RXRX, TEM, ONT.L) and 8 private peers in the Biotech & Health sector, with direct stage-matched comparables including Colossal Biosciences ($10.3B), Chai Discovery ($3.8B), and New Limit ($3.1B).\n\nTwo triangulation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis applies a 1.7x step-up multiplier typical of Series C advancement to the $700M capital raised proxy, yielding $1.2B. Peer-median valuation across the 3 same-sector, same-stage comparables produces $3.8B, with the peer range spanning $3.1B to $10.3B. Public-comp anchoring via price-to-sales multiples (sector median 5.5x) cannot be applied due to absence of revenue disclosure, standard for private companies. The two applicable methods produce materially divergent results, reflecting both the wide dispersion in late-stage biotech valuations and uncertainty around Ultima's relative market position.\n\nThe triangulated valuation range is $1.0B to $4.4B, with a median of $2.5B. The wide spread reflects tension between the conservative stage-based approach and the elevated peer comparables. Key uncertainties include revenue traction, intellectual property strength relative to peers, and whether peer valuations reflect justified differentiation or sector effusion. Further disclosure of capital deployment efficiency would narrow this range.",
