      "narrative": "Heart Aerospace is a Series B-stage space and aerospace company founded by Anders and Klara Forslund that has raised $185M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comp universe of 5 public-market peers (Rocket Lab, Planet Labs, Lunar Resources, AST SpaceMobile, Satellite Lab) and 8 private-stage companies in the same sector, including Sierra Space, Cowboy Space Corporation, Varda Space Industries, Aalyria, and Skyryse.\n\nTwo quantitative methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis applies a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical of Series B advancement to the $185M total raised proxy, implying a valuation of $352M. Peer-median analysis across five same-sector and same/adjacent-stage comparables yields a median valuation of $1.5B, with a range from $1.1B (Skyryse) to $8.0B (Sierra Space). Public-comp anchoring via price-to-sales multiples cannot be applied, as Heart Aerospace's revenue is not disclosed.\n\nThe triangulated range across both applicable methods spans $299M (low) to $1.7B (high), with a median of $926M. The wide dispersion reflects material stage and maturity heterogeneity among the peer set\u2014Sierra Space trades at a significant premium while earlier-stage peers cluster lower. Key uncertainties include Heart Aerospace's revenue trajectory, path to profitability, and competitive positioning within a densely funded sector.",
