      "narrative": "VEIR is a Series B climate and energy technology company founded by Tim Heidel that has raised $117M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a peer set of three same-sector, same/adjacent-stage private companies (KoBold Metals at $3.0B, Electric Hydrogen at $1.0B, and Amogy at $700M), supplemented by a broader comparable universe of eight private peers and one public comparable (Lonza, ticker LNZA).\n\nTwo triangulation methods are applied. Stage-progression analysis applies a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical of Series B advancement to the $117M total raised proxy, yielding $222M. Peer-median valuation anchors to the median of the three-company comparable set at $1.0B, with a range spanning $700M to $3.0B. This method reflects recent market precedent for funded climate-tech companies at similar development stages.\n\nThe combined analysis supports a valuation range of $189M (low) to $1.1B (high), with a median of $611M. The wide range\u2014spanning nearly a full order of magnitude\u2014reflects material uncertainty inherent in early-stage climate technology valuations. Key variables affecting positioning within this range include technology maturity, pathway to commercialization, addressable market validation, and fundraising momentum relative to peer cohort. The stage-progression method anchors the low end; peer comparables dominate the high end, suggesting market multiples for proven-stage climate platforms substantially exceed simple capital-raised multiples.",
