      "narrative": "Aerospacelab is a Series B-stage space and aerospace company that has raised \u20ac200M+. The valuation analysis draws on a peer set of five same-sector, same/adjacent-stage private comparables: Sierra Space ($8.0B, Series C), Cowboy Space Corporation ($2.0B, Series B), Varda Space Industries ($1.5B, Series C), Aalyria ($1.3B, Series B), and Skyryse ($1.1B, Series C). Public-comp anchoring was not applicable due to the absence of disclosed revenue figures.\n\nThe peer-median method is the applicable triangulation approach here. The median valuation across the five comparables is $1.5B, with observed valuations ranging from $1.1B to $8.0B. This wide dispersion reflects stage variance (two peers are Series C) and heterogeneity in underlying business models within the aerospace sector. Given Aerospacelab's Series B positioning and capital raised, the peer-median of $1.5B serves as the primary anchor.\n\nThe triangulated valuation range is $1.3B\u2013$1.7B, with a median point estimate of $1.5B. This range reflects the observed interquartile spread within the peer cohort. Key uncertainties include revenue scale and traction relative to the comparison set\u2014unavailable for the target and critical to validating stage-appropriate positioning\u2014and the inherent heterogeneity of aerospace business models, which produces a peer valuation spread exceeding 7x between minimum and maximum.",
