      "narrative": "Reverion is a Series B climate and energy company that has raised $79M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comparable universe of nine private frontier-tech companies and one public peer, primarily within advanced energy infrastructure and materials.\n\nTwo methods triangulate the valuation. Stage-progression analysis applies a 1.9x multiplier to the $79M in total capital raised, implying a $150M valuation consistent with typical Series B advancement. Peer-median analysis references three same-sector, same-stage comparables: KoBold Metals ($3.0B, Series C), Electric Hydrogen ($1.0B, Series C), and Amogy ($700M, Series C). The median valuation of this peer set is $1.0B, with a range of $700M to $3.0B.\n\nTriangulating these methods yields a low estimate of $128M, a median of $575M, and a high of $1.1B. The substantial spread reflects material uncertainty inherent in early-stage deep-tech valuation. The stage-progression method anchors the conservative end, while the peer-median approach\u2014drawing from slightly later-stage comparables\u2014pulls the range higher. Key uncertainties include the maturity of Reverion's core technology relative to peers, customer pipeline development, and the trajectory of capital costs in the decarbonization hardware market. A valuation in the $400M\u2013$700M range appears most defensible pending disclosure of customer contracts or near-term revenue visibility.",
