      "narrative": "44.01 is a Series A climate and energy company that has raised $37M to date. The valuation universe for climate and energy includes one public comparable (LNZA) and eight private peers spanning fusion, battery recycling, solid-state batteries, critical minerals, and hydrogen production. However, narrow-set peer analysis proved inapplicable: zero same-stage or adjacent-stage comparables with sufficient valuation data existed within the Climate & Energy sector, falling short of the minimum three-datapoint threshold required for reliable median derivation.\n\nStage-progression analysis anchors the valuation. Using $37M in total raised as a proxy for current post-money value, a typical 2.0x step-up multiplier applied to Series A companies yields $74M. This method captures the expected valuation lift between early institutional rounds and subsequent growth stages, though it assumes 44.01 tracks median progression velocity within its cohort. No other triangulation method produced sufficient data quality.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $63M to $85M, centered at $74M. The range reflects \u00b115% sensitivity around the stage-progression anchor, accounting for variance in capital deployment efficiency and market conditions within climate tech. Key uncertainties include the absence of direct peer revenue or unit economics data, which would refine stage-appropriate valuation multiples, and the nascent state of the climate tech public market, limiting benchmarking precision. Additional operational and commercialization milestones will be necessary to validate this range at next financing.",
