      "narrative": "Nomagic is a Series B robotics and manufacturing company that has raised $97M to date. Valuation analysis draws on a universe of 9 private peers and 1 public comparable, spanning similar-stage companies in the Robotics & Manufacturing sector including Bedrock Robotics, Dexterity, Hadrian, and Nimble Robotics.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression, using the $97M total raised as a proxy baseline and applying a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical for Series B advancement, implies a valuation of $184M. Peer-median analysis across the four comparable companies yields a median valuation of $1.6B, with a range of $1.0B to $1.8B. The disparity between these methods reflects the heterogeneity within the robotics sector at this stage.\n\nSynthesizing both approaches produces a triangulated range of $157M (low) to $1.9B (high), with a median of $905M. The wide band reflects material uncertainty in the appropriate peer set and stage-progression trajectory for Nomagic. Key unknowns include revenue run-rate relative to comparables, the company's capital efficiency, and whether stage-progression or peer multiples better anchor valuation for an unfunded round. The peer-median approach carries more weight given market evidence, but the low-end scenario assumes minimal premium to capital deployed.",
