      "narrative": "Fractile is a Series B semiconductor company founded by Walter Goodwin that has raised $220M to date. Valuation benchmarking draws on a peer universe of 11 comparable companies\u20143 public (ALAB, NVDA, AMD) and 8 private players spanning chip design and AI infrastructure, including SambaNova Systems, Etched, d-Matrix, Positron AI, and DEEPX.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis uses the $220M total raised as a valuation proxy and applies a 1.9x multiplier typical for Series B advancement, implying $418M. Peer-median analysis examines five same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables with valuations ranging from $529M (DEEPX, Series C) to $11.0B (SambaNova, Series A), yielding a median of $2.0B. The wide range reflects heterogeneous growth trajectories and funding environments across the semiconductor frontier-tech space.\n\nTriangulating both methods produces a valuation range of $355M (low) to $2.3B (high), with a median of $1.2B. Stage-progression anchors the floor; peer median anchors upside. Key uncertainties include the timing and trajectory of revenue growth, competitive positioning within a crowded chip-design market, and the sustainability of recent private-market multiples in semiconductors given macro volatility. The wide peer range ($529M\u2013$11.0B) itself signals limited consensus on comparable valuations at this stage.",
