      "narrative": "Cambridge Aerospace, a Series A defense-tech company founded by Steven Barrett and Chris Sylvan, has raised $136M to date and is currently fundraising for $200M additional capital. The valuation analysis draws on a comparable universe of 10 same-sector peers at Series A and adjacent stages in Defense & Security, comprising 2 public companies (DRSHF, IDEAFORGE.NS) and 8 private firms including Anduril Industries, Helsing, and Shield AI. The peer median valuation stands at $1.0B, with a range spanning $125M to $3.0B.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, using the $136M total raised as a valuation proxy and applying a standard 2.0x Series A-to-next-stage step-up multiplier, yields $272M. Peer-median analysis anchors to the $1.0B median across the 10-company comp set. The divergence between these methods reflects typical early-stage valuation dispersion in frontier defense tech, where company-specific technical maturity, customer traction, and founder pedigree drive wide valuation spreads.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $231M (low) to $1.1B (high), with a median of $636M. Key uncertainties include the degree to which Cambridge Aerospace's technical capabilities and customer commitments justify positioning above or below the peer median, and whether the broader defense-tech cohort's current valuations reflect sustainable market fundamentals or sector-specific momentum.",
