      "narrative": "Cailabs is a Series C\u2013stage space and aerospace company that has raised \u20ac57M+ to date. The peer set for valuation consists of three private Series C companies in the same sector: Sierra Space ($8.0B), Varda Space Industries ($1.5B), and Skyryse ($1.1B). Public comps in Space & Aerospace number five (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) with a median EV/Sales multiple of 23.9x, though this method cannot be applied without the target's revenue figure.\n\nPeer-median triangulation is the applicable method here. The three same-stage, same-sector private comparables yield a median valuation of $1.5B, with a range spanning $1.1B to $8.0B. This range reflects material heterogeneity within the Series C space tech cohort\u2014Sierra Space trades at a premium, likely reflecting downstream integration or a distinct market position, while Skyryse and Varda cluster closer to the lower bound.\n\nAnalysis supports a valuation range of $1.3B to $1.7B, centered at $1.5B. This median-centered range reflects the most stable signal from peer positioning. Key uncertainties include the wide peer dispersion ($1.1B\u2013$8.0B), which suggests significant valuation variance even within a narrow stage and sector filter, and the absence of revenue or growth rate data to anchor relative positioning within the peer set. The public comp method remains unavailable pending disclosure of Cailabs' revenue.",
