      "narrative": "iQPS is a publicly listed Space & Aerospace company founded by Tetsuo Yasaka, Akira Sakurai, and Kunihiro Funakoshi. The valuation universe comprises 5 public peers (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private comparables including Planet Labs, Astroscale, SpaceX, Sierra Space, and Impulse Space, totaling 13 datapoints across the sector.\n\nTwo standard triangulation methods were evaluated. Peer-Median analysis proved inapplicable due to insufficient narrow peer filtration: while 11 same-sector peers exist, only 2 matched same-stage criteria, yielding an n below the minimum threshold of 3. Restricting to adjacent-stage or similar-valuation-tier comparables yielded zero datapoints, making sector-wide median anchoring unreliable. Public-Comp Anchoring was also inapplicable; the Space & Aerospace sector median Price-to-Sales multiple is 23.9x across the 6 public tickers identified, but iQPS's revenue was not on file, preventing multiplication-based valuation.\n\nNo triangulated valuation range can be supported from the available data. The constraint is informational rather than methodological: iQPS's audited revenue and near-term financial guidance are prerequisites for either revenue-multiple or earnings-based anchoring. Until disclosure or reliable estimates emerge, quantitative valuation relies on private-round benchmarking against Astroscale, Planet Labs, and comparable-stage funded entities\u2014data not provided here. Engagement with company management on recent contracting activity and revenue run-rate is necessary to proceed.",
