      "narrative": "Axelspace is a Series D-stage space and aerospace company founded by Yuya Nakamura. The valuation analysis draws from a comparable universe of 4 private peers in the same sector and stage, supplemented by reference to 5 public Space & Aerospace equities (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 additional private companies for context.\n\nThe peer-median method is the primary applicable approach. A median valuation of $1.9B emerges from 4 same-sector, same/adjacent-stage peers: Apex Space ($2.3B, Series D), Sierra Space ($8.0B, Series C), Varda Space Industries ($1.5B, Series C), and Skyryse ($1.1B, Series C). This yields a range of $1.1B to $8.0B across the sample. Public-comp anchoring cannot be applied absent disclosed revenue for Axelspace; the sector median P/S multiple stands at 23.9x across 6 public tickers, but remains unusable without the target's top-line figure.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $1.6B to $2.2B, centered on $1.9B. Key uncertainties include the wide dispersion in peer valuations ($1.1B\u2013$8.0B), reflecting stage heterogeneity and company-specific factors within the peer set. The absence of revenue data precludes public-market cross-validation. Stage advancement and product maturity relative to peers remain material drivers of placement within the indicated range.",
