      "narrative": "Pale Blue is a Series A space and aerospace company founded by Jun Asakawa and Yuichi Nakagawa that has raised $7.5M in equity plus $27M in non-dilutive grant funding. The valuation analysis draws on a landscape of 5 public comparables (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private peers including SpaceX, Sierra Space, and Planet Labs.\n\nOf three triangulation methods tested, only stage-progression proved applicable. Using total raised ($7.5M) as a valuation proxy and applying a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical for Series A advancement yields $15M. Peer-median analysis was inapplicable due to insufficient same-stage or adjacent-stage comparables with similar valuation tiers in the narrow space sector universe. Public-comp anchoring could not be executed because the target's revenue is not disclosed, a constraint endemic to private companies; the median P/S for the public set is 23.9x across six tickers, but lacks an operational denominator.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $13M to $17M, centered on $15M. This narrow band reflects dependence on a single method and the structural opacity of early-stage aerospace valuations. Key uncertainties include the absence of disclosed revenue (limiting cross-sector benchmarking), the limited peer cohort at identical stage and scale, and the role of non-dilutive capital ($27M grants) in de-risking the equity round and potentially justifying uplift above the derived multiple.",
