      "narrative": "Telexistence, a Series B robotics and manufacturing company that has raised $170M+, is valued here against a comp universe of 9 private peers and 1 public comparable (277810.KQ). The private peer set includes four same-sector, same/adjacent-stage companies: Bedrock Robotics ($1.8B Series B), Dexterity ($1.6B Series B), Hadrian ($1.6B Series C), and Nimble Robotics ($1.0B Series C).\n\nTwo triangulation methods are applicable. The stage-progression method applies a 1.9x step-up multiplier to the $170M total raised proxy, implying a $323M valuation. The peer-median method derives a $1.6B valuation from the four-company peer cohort, which spans a $1.0B\u2013$1.8B range. These two approaches reflect materially different assumptions about Telexistence's relative positioning within the robotics financing landscape.\n\nThe triangulated analysis yields a low of $275M, a median of $974M, and a high of $1.9B. The wide spread reflects fundamental tension between a capital-raised proxy (which anchors the lower bound) and peer comparables (which anchor the upper bound). Key uncertainties center on the degree to which Telexistence's technology, customer traction, or team warrant valuation parity with established peers like Bedrock or Dexterity, and whether stage-progression assumptions or peer benchmarking better reflects market sentiment for this asset class.",
