      "narrative": "Terra Drone is a publicly listed company in the Drones & Autonomous sector, having completed an IPO on the Tokyo exchange. The valuation analysis faces a significant constraint: the Drones & Autonomous sector contains only five identifiable peers, none of which satisfy standard comparability filters for stage alignment or valuation tier clustering required for reliable peer-median analysis.\n\nThe peer-median triangulation method is not applicable. While six private companies operate in the same sector\u2014including Zipline, Joby Aviation, Nuro, Archer Aviation, and Elroy Air\u2014none meet the threshold of three or more comparables at the same development stage or adjacent stage with similar valuation tiers. The absence of public comps in this sector further constrains traditional multiple-based approaches. Applying an all-sector median would introduce material noise and misrepresent Terra Drone's market position.\n\nGiven these data limitations, conventional valuation triangulation cannot be performed with statistical confidence. The analysis would require additional methodologies such as discounted cash flow analysis with transparent assumptions, analysis of Terra Drone's specific financial performance relative to the fragmented private peer set, or market structure analysis of the Japanese public markets for nascent autonomous technology companies. The key uncertainty is the lack of a sufficiently dense comparable set; any valuation conclusion without supplementary methods would rest on limited quantitative grounding.",
