      "narrative": "Raphe mPhibr is a Series B defense and security company founded by Vivek and Vikash Mishra that has raised $145M+. The valuation analysis draws on a comp universe of 10 total peers\u20142 public (DRSHF, IDEAFORGE.NS) and 8 private\u2014all operating in the same sector and stage.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. The stage-progression approach uses the $145M total raised as a baseline proxy and applies a 1.9x multiplier typical of Series B advancement, yielding $276M. The peer-median method examines 7 same-sector, same-stage private companies\u2014Dream Security ($3.0B), Harmattan AI ($1.4B), Code Metal ($1.2B), Castelion ($1.0B), Defense Unicorns ($1.0B), and two others\u2014producing a median valuation of $1.0B with a range of $300M to $3.0B.\n\nSynthesizing these methods yields a triangulated range of $234M (low) to $1.1B (high), with a median of $638M. The stage-progression method anchors the lower bound while peer comparables suggest material upside. Key uncertainties include wide dispersion within the peer set ($300M\u2013$3.0B) and the appropriate weighting of public comps versus private peers. The median estimate of $638M reflects a middle position but should be stress-tested against relative product maturity, revenue scale, and customer concentration relative to the named peer set.",
