      "narrative": "Newspace Research is a Series B-stage frontier-tech company operating in Defense & Security, founded by Sameer Joshi, with $73.2M in total capital raised to date. The valuation assessment draws on a comparable universe of 10 peers: 2 public companies (DRSHF, IDEAFORGE.NS) and 8 private firms, including Dream Security, Harmattan AI, Code Metal, Castelion, and Defense Unicorns.\n\nTwo valuation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis uses the company's $73.2M raised as a base proxy and applies a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical of Series B advancement, yielding $139M. Peer-median analysis references 7 same-sector, same-stage comparables with valuations ranging from $300M to $3.0B; the median across this set is $1.0B. The peer cohort exhibits material dispersion, reflective of differentiated technology maturity and market positioning within the Defense & Security sector.\n\nTriangulation across these two methods produces a valuation range of $118M (low) to $1.1B (high), with a median of $570M. The wide spread\u2014spanning nearly one order of magnitude\u2014reflects meaningful uncertainty around Newspace Research's positioning relative to peers. Key drivers of valuation uncertainty include revenue traction and growth rate relative to the peer set, product-market fit in defense applications, and customer concentration. The stage-progression method anchors conservatively to capital deployed, while peer-median reflects market-observed pricing but carries risk if Newspace's fundamentals deviate from peer norms.",
