      "narrative": "Mindgrove Technologies is a Series A semiconductor company founded by Shashwath TR and Sharan Srinivas J that has raised \u20b985 crore (~$10M) to date. The valuation analysis draws from a sector universe of 11 same-stage and adjacent-stage peers in Chips & Semiconductors, supplemented by a broader comp set of 3 public peers (ALAB, NVDA, AMD) and 8 private peers including SambaNova Systems, Cerebras, PsiQuantum, Etched, and Tenstorrent.\n\nThe peer-median method is not applicable here due to insufficient narrow peer clustering. While 11 same-sector peers exist, fewer than 3 datapoints satisfy the filters of same-stage, adjacent-stage, or similar-valuation-tier classification simultaneously. Applying an all-sector median would introduce material noise given the heterogeneity of semiconductor subsectors and stage distributions. Public comparables present additional challenges: NVDA and AMD trade at valuations reflecting mature scale and profitability, while ALAB represents a different architecture segment. The private peer set (SambaNova, Cerebras, Tenstorrent et al.) provides directional reference for frontier chip companies, though most are further progressed than Series A.\n\nThe sparse peer landscape and stage-specific valuation dynamics preclude a robust triangulated range at present. A credible valuation would require either: (1) deeper operational data on Mindgrove's chip architecture, IP defensibility, and go-to-market traction; or (2) expansion of comparable filtering to capture more Series A and early-stage semiconductor plays. Current data supports only qualitative positioning relative to the private peer cohort, not quantitative range estimation.",
