      "narrative": "Qedma is a Series A quantum computing company founded by Asif Sinay, Netanel Lindner, and Dorit Aharonov, having raised $26M+ to date. The quantum computing sector comprises 3 public comparables (IONQ, RGTI, QBTS) and 8 private peers including Quantinuum, IonQ, D-Wave Quantum, Rigetti Computing, and Infleqtion.\n\nPeer-median valuation analysis was not applicable due to insufficient same-stage and adjacent-stage comparables in the quantum computing universe\u2014while 5 sector peers exist, none met the three-datapoint threshold required for statistical reliability. Stage-progression methodology proved the only applicable triangulation approach. Using total raised of $26M as a proxy for post-money valuation and applying a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical for progression from Series A to the next funding round yields an implied valuation of $52M.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $44M to $60M, with a median estimate of $52M. Key uncertainties stem from the narrow and heterogeneous peer set in quantum computing\u2014the sector includes hardware platforms, software/algorithm providers, and hybrid-classical systems at varying technology readiness levels, limiting direct comparability. Additionally, the absence of recent, closely-matched private financings constrains calibration of the stage-progression multiplier. Investors should weight this valuation as illustrative pending access to more granular comparable transaction data or management guidance on burn rate and capital efficiency metrics.",
