      "narrative": "Speedata is a Series B-stage semiconductor company founded by Jonathan Friedmann, Dan Charash, Rafi Shalom, Itai Incze, Yoav Etsion, and Dani Voitsechov. The company has raised $114M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a comp universe of 11 private companies and 3 public peers (ALAB, NVDA, AMD) in the chips and semiconductors sector.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, using total raised ($114M) as a proxy for current valuation and applying a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical for Series B advancement, yields $217M. Peer-median methodology across five same-sector and same/adjacent-stage comparables\u2014SambaNova Systems ($11.0B Series A), Etched ($5.0B Series C), d-Matrix ($2.0B Series C), Positron AI ($1.0B Series B), and DEEPX ($529M Series C)\u2014produces a median of $2.0B, with a range of $529M to $11.0B.\n\nThe combined analysis supports a valuation range of $184M (low) to $2.3B (high), with a median of $1.1B. The 12x spread between low and high reflects material uncertainty inherent in peer comparables, particularly the wide dispersion in stage-adjusted valuations within the frontier semiconductor cohort. The peer-median method is heavily weighted by later-stage, higher-valuation outliers; stage-progression offers a more conservative floor anchored to capital deployed. Key uncertainties include the target's product differentiation relative to the sampled peers and execution risk at Series B.",
