      "narrative": "Simera Sense is a Series B-stage space and aerospace company founded by Johann du Toit, having raised $16.3M+ to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comparable universe of 5 public companies (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private peers including Sierra Space, Cowboy Space Corporation, Varda Space Industries, Aalyria, and Skyryse.\n\nTwo valuation methods proved applicable. Stage-progression analysis, using the $16M raised as a proxy base value and applying a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical of Series B advancement, implies a valuation of $31M. Peer-median analysis across five same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables yields a median valuation of $1.5B, with a range spanning $1.1B (Skyryse) to $8.0B (Sierra Space). The public-comp anchoring method, which would apply a 23.9x sector price-to-sales median, cannot be executed due to absence of target revenue disclosure, typical for private companies.\n\nThe triangulation of applicable methods produces a valuation range of $26M (low) to $1.7B (high), with a median of $765M. The wide dispersion reflects inherent uncertainty in early-stage aerospace valuation, where peer outcomes vary substantially by technological maturity, market traction, and capital efficiency. The stage-progression method suggests conservative floor valuation; peer comparables anchor the upper bound. Key uncertainties include revenue run-rate, customer concentration, and technology risk relative to the peer cohort.",
