      "narrative": "Morpheus Space is a Series A-stage space and aerospace company founded by Daniel Bock and Istv\u00e1n L\u0151rincz, having raised $43M+ to date. The valuation landscape includes five public comparables (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) trading at a median 23.9x revenue multiple, and eight private peers including SpaceX, Sierra Space, and Planet Labs. However, the narrowness of same-stage precedents in this sector limits multi-method triangulation.\n\nStage-progression methodology, the sole applicable approach, anchors valuation to the $43M total capital raised as a proxy floor and applies a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A advancement. This yields $86M. Peer-median analysis cannot proceed\u2014while 11 same-sector private companies exist, none of the filtered cohorts (same-stage, adjacent-stage, or similar-tier) reached the three-point minimum required for robust medianization. Public-comp anchoring via P/S multiples is inapplicable without disclosed revenue figures, standard opacity in private-company datasets.\n\nThe analysis supports a median valuation of $86M, bracketed conservatively between $73M and $99M to reflect Stage-progression method variance. Key uncertainties include the absence of comparable private transactions at identical stage and tier, lack of revenue disclosure precluding multiple-based validation, and the sector-specific illiquidity and long development cycles inherent to aerospace. The single-method conclusion warrants validation against operational milestones and future funding rounds.",
