      "narrative": "Orbem is a Series B-stage biotech and health company that has raised \u20ac55.5M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a peer set of four private companies in the same sector and stage vicinity, supplemented by three public biotech comparables (RXRX, TEM, ONT.L) used for directional context only.\n\nThe peer-median method is the primary applicable triangulation approach. The four private comparables\u2014Colossal Biosciences ($10.3B, Series C), Chai Discovery ($3.8B, Series C), New Limit ($3.1B, Series C), and Eikon Therapeutics ($539M, Series B)\u2014yield a median valuation of $3.5B. This range spans from $539M at the low end to $10.3B at the high end, reflecting material variance within the cohort. Public biotech comps trade at a 5.5x median price-to-sales multiple, but this method cannot be applied without Orbem's disclosed revenue, which is not available for private-stage targets.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $2.9B to $4.0B, centered on the peer median of $3.5B. Key uncertainties include the composition of the peer set\u2014only one direct Series B comparator exists in the sample\u2014and the absence of revenue or profitability data to ground relative valuation metrics. The wide dispersion in peer valuations ($539M to $10.3B) reflects heterogeneity in technology maturity and capital efficiency within the frontier biotech space.",
