      "narrative": "Asterra, a Series A-stage Space & Aerospace company founded by Lauren Guy, has raised $20M+ to date. The valuation universe consists of 6 public comparables (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private peers including SpaceX, Sierra Space, and Planet Labs, though narrow peer clustering at identical stage and valuation tier remains sparse within the sector.\n\nStage-progression analysis applies a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A advancement, anchoring to the $20M raised as a proxy for current valuation and implying $40M post-valuation. Peer-median triangulation was not applicable\u2014while 11 same-sector peers exist, fewer than 3 companies met simultaneous same-stage, adjacent-stage, and similar-tier filters, making sector-wide median unreliable. Public-comp anchoring could not proceed without disclosed revenue; the Space & Aerospace sector median P/S of 23.9x across 6 public tickers remains inert without target financials.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $34M (low) to $46M (high), with a median point of $40M. This estimate derives from a single applicable method and carries material uncertainty. Key risks include limited private-market comparability at this early stage and absence of revenue or margin data, which would sharpen public-market anchoring. Further due diligence on unit economics and capital efficiency within the cohort would materially improve conviction.",
