      "narrative": "Vention is a Series C robotics and manufacturing company founded by Etienne Lacroix and Max Windisch, having raised $95M+ to date. The valuation analysis draws from a comp universe of 9 private robotics firms at Series B through Series D stages\u2014including Exotec ($2.0B, Series D), Hadrian ($1.6B, Series C), and Nimble Robotics ($1.0B, Series C)\u2014plus one public comparable.\n\nTwo triangulation methods are applied. Stage-progression analysis uses the $95M total raised as a proxy base and applies a 1.7x multiplier typical of Series C advancement, yielding $162M. Peer-median analysis across five same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables (Exotec, Bedrock Robotics, Dexterity, Hadrian, and Nimble Robotics) establishes a median valuation of $1.6B, with a range of $1.0B to $2.0B. The substantial gap between methods reflects stage-progression's conservative reliance on historical capital raised versus peer multiples embedded in recent private market transactions.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a range of $137M (low) to $1.9B (high), with a median of $906M. This wide band reflects genuine uncertainty around Vention's commercial traction relative to peers. Reconciliation hinges on clarifying revenue scale, growth trajectory, and competitive positioning within the robotics automation segment relative to Hadrian and Nimble Robotics, which command $1.6B\u2013$1.0B at identical stage.",
