      "narrative": "SambaNova Systems, a Series A semiconductor company, is valued at $11.0B post-money following $1.1B in total capital raised. Valuation analysis draws from a comp universe of 11 peers across Chips & Semiconductors\u20143 public (ALAB, NVDA, AMD) and 8 private\u2014with particular relevance to 5 directly comparable private companies: Cerebras, PsiQuantum, Etched, Tenstorrent, and Rebellions.\n\nTwo triangulation methods are applied. Stage-Progression anchors to the $11.0B last post-money valuation and applies a typical 2.0x step-up multiplier for advancement to the next funding round, implying $22.0B. Peer-Median analysis across 6 same-sector comparable companies yields a median valuation of $3.9B, with a range spanning $2.3B (Rebellions) to $39.2B (Cerebras). The wide peer dispersion reflects heterogeneous maturity stages and market positioning within the sector.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $3.3B (low) to $25.3B (high), with a median of $12.9B. The current $11.0B valuation sits near the midpoint, consistent with stage-relative positioning but materially above the peer median. Key uncertainties include the relevance of the Cerebras outlier at $39.2B (public, more mature) versus earlier-stage private comparables, and the execution risk inherent in Series A-stage semiconductor ventures. The peer median suggests material downside risk, while stage-progression supports upside to $22B if development and commercialization milestones are achieved.",
