      "narrative": "Credo Semiconductor, a public-stage chip design company founded by William Brennan and Lawrence Cheng and taken public via IPO in 2022, is evaluated against a peer universe of 3 same-sector public comparables in Chips & Semiconductors, supplemented by 8 private frontier-tech peers including SambaNova Systems and PsiQuantum.\n\nThe peer-median method, the applicable triangulation approach given available data, anchors valuation to three public comparables: Cerebras at $39.2B, Ouster at $2.3B, and Aeva Technologies at $1.1B. The median across this set yields $2.3B, with a range spanning $1.1B to $39.2B. This wide dispersion reflects heterogeneity in chip subsector maturity and capital efficiency across the peer group. The peer-median implied valuation of $2.3B serves as the central anchor.\n\nThe triangulated valuation range is $1.9B to $2.6B (median $2.3B), derived solely from peer-median methodology. This range sits substantially below Credo's current public market valuation of approximately $35.8B, suggesting material divergence between public market pricing and comparable-company analysis. Key uncertainties include the relevance of the three public peers\u2014Cerebras's $39.2B valuation represents a significant outlier\u2014and the absence of revenue, profitability, or growth metrics to refine peer selection and weighting. The narrow methodological foundation (one approach) limits confidence in the range absent additional data on Credo's financial performance or strategic positioning.",
