      "narrative": "Stratolaunch is a private-stage Space & Aerospace company with a comp universe spanning 5 public tickers (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private peers including SpaceX, Sierra Space, and Planet Labs. The sector includes 11 same-sector peers total, though few operate at directly comparable stage and scale.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were evaluated. Peer-median analysis proved inapplicable: while 11 Space & Aerospace peers exist, filtering for same-stage, adjacent-stage, or similar valuation-tier peers yielded fewer than 3 datapoints, making a narrow median unreliable. Public-comp anchoring was also inapplicable because Stratolaunch's revenue is not on file\u2014standard practice for private companies\u2014and therefore a price-to-sales multiple cannot be derived. The public Space & Aerospace sector carries a median P/S of 23.9x across the 6-ticker universe, but applying this multiple requires disclosed revenue, which is unavailable.\n\nWithout quantifiable revenue data or a sufficiently dense peer cohort meeting stage and tier filters, this analysis cannot support a specific valuation range via standard triangulation. A credible valuation would require either (1) Stratolaunch's disclosed or estimated revenue; (2) deeper access to private comparables' financial metrics; or (3) application of venture cost-to-development milestones. The frontier-stage, capital-intensive nature of aerospace compounds uncertainty around comparable company selection.",
