      "narrative": "Scout Space is a Series A-stage space and aerospace company founded by Eric Ingram and Sergio Gallucci, having raised $18M to date. The valuation universe for Space & Aerospace comprises 5 public comparables (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private peers including SpaceX, Sierra Space, and Planet Labs.\n\nOnly one valuation method is reliably applicable given available data. Stage-progression analysis uses the $18M total raised as a baseline valuation proxy and applies a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical for Series A advancement, yielding $36M. The peer-median method cannot be applied: while 11 same-sector peers exist, filtering for identical or adjacent stage and similar valuation tier yields fewer than three datapoints, making any extrapolation unreliable. Public-comp anchoring cannot be executed because Scout Space's revenue is not disclosed; the Space & Aerospace sector median P/S of 23.9x across the five public tickers cannot be applied without this input.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $31M to $41M, centered at $36M. This range reflects \u00b115% variance around the stage-progression result. The primary uncertainty stems from the single-method foundation: deeper revenue visibility or access to a tighter set of late-stage private comparables would substantially strengthen conviction. The public-market median P/S of 23.9x suggests later-stage multiples in the sector are elevated, but application to an early-revenue Series A company would require revenue disclosure and explicit stage-adjustment assumptions.",
