      "narrative": "Genesis Therapeutics is a Series B-stage biotech company that has raised $280M+ to date. The valuation analysis draws on a universe of 8 private peers and 3 public comparables in the Biotech & Health sector, including adjacent-stage companies like Colossal Biosciences ($10.3B), Chai Discovery ($3.8B), New Limit ($3.1B), and Eikon Therapeutics ($539M).\n\nTwo triangulation methods prove applicable. The stage-progression method, using $280M total raised as a proxy baseline and applying a 1.9x Series B step-up multiplier, yields $532M. The peer-median method across the four same-sector comparables produces $3.5B, reflecting a wide range of $539M to $10.3B. Public-comp anchoring via price-to-sales multiples (median 5.5x across RXRX, TEM, and ONT.L) cannot be applied absent the target's revenue figures. \n\nThese two methods triangulate to a median valuation of $2.0B, with a low-end anchor of $452M and a high-end ceiling of $4.0B. The wide dispersion reflects material uncertainty around stage-appropriate valuation within the peer set\u2014specifically, the influence of outliers like Colossal on the median. Key drivers of upside within this range include clinical-stage progression and partner validation; downside risks include execution timelines and capital intensity typical of early-stage therapeutic development.",
