      "narrative": "BRINC Drones, a Series C defense and security drone manufacturer founded by Blake Resnick, presents a valuation challenge given the sector's wide dispersion. The analysis draws on a peer universe of 12 same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables, comprising 2 public companies (DRSHF, IDEAFORGE.NS) and 8 private firms including Quantum-Systems ($8.0B, Series C), Helsing ($18.0B, Series D), and Saronic ($9.2B, Series D).\n\nTwo triangulation methods are applicable. Stage-progression anchors to BRINC's $157M total raised proxy, applying a 1.7x step-up multiplier typical of Series C advancement, yielding $267M. Peer-median analysis across the 12-company comp set yields $1.8B, with a range spanning $300M to $18.0B. The wide peer dispersion reflects heterogeneous technology maturity, customer concentration, and pathway to defense contracting within the sector.\n\nThe triangulated midpoint valuation is $1.0B, supported by a low-end estimate of $227M and high-end of $2.0B. The gap between stage-progression ($267M) and peer-median ($1.8B) reflects material uncertainty around BRINC's competitive positioning relative to better-capitalized or further-advanced peers. Key sensitivities include customer concentration in U.S. defense procurement, regulatory pathway clarity, and realized margins on government contracts. A Series C range of $600M\u2013$1.3B balances stage mechanics against peer comparables while acknowledging execution risk.",
