      "narrative": "Deep Sentinel, a Series B defense and security company founded by David Selinger, has raised $55M to date. The valuation assessment draws on a comparables universe of 10 peers: 2 public companies (DRSHF, IDEAFORGE.NS) and 8 private firms, including Dream Security, Harmattan AI, Code Metal, Castelion, and Defense Unicorns.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis uses the $55M raised as a valuation proxy and applies a 1.9x multiplier typical of Series B to subsequent-stage transitions, implying $104M. Peer-median analysis examines 7 same-sector, same-stage comparables, which exhibit a median valuation of $1.0B with a range of $300M to $3.0B. The peer sample includes Castelion and Defense Unicorns both valued at $1.0B, Harmattan AI at $1.4B, and Dream Security at $3.0B.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $89M to $1.1B, with a median of $552M. The wide spread reflects substantial variance in the peer set: stage-progression methodology implies a more conservative valuation anchored to capital deployed, while peer-median reflects current market pricing for similarly-staged defense-tech companies. Key uncertainties include Deep Sentinel's relative position on revenue, growth rate, and defensibility versus named peers, as well as the representativeness of the comparable set given the nascent and heterogeneous defense-tech sector.",
