      "narrative": "LuxWall is a Series B climate and energy technology company founded by Scott Thomsen that has raised $84M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comp universe of nine private firms and one public company (LNZA) operating in the same sector, with particular focus on three same-sector, same/adjacent-stage peers: KoBold Metals ($3.0B Series C), Electric Hydrogen ($1.0B Series C), and Amogy ($700M Series C).\n\nTwo triangulation methods are applicable. The stage-progression method applies a typical Series B step-up multiplier of 1.9x to the $84M raised proxy, implying a valuation of $160M. The peer-median method references the median valuation across the three comparable companies at $1.0B, with a range spanning $700M to $3.0B. These methods produce materially different results, reflecting differences in company maturity and market positioning within the cohort.\n\nSynthesizing both approaches yields a triangulated range of $136M (low) to $1.1B (high), with a median of $580M. The wide spread reflects genuine uncertainty about LuxWall's position relative to later-stage peers. Key drivers of valuation within this range include capital efficiency relative to comparables, time to revenue inflection, and customer validation metrics not present in available data. The peer-median approach anchors toward higher valuations, while stage-based progression suggests a more conservative floor.",
