      "narrative": "Cambium, a Series B robotics and manufacturing company founded by Simon Waddington and Stephan Herrera, has raised $127M+ to date. Valuation assessment relies on a peer set of 4 same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparable companies (Bedrock Robotics, Dexterity, Hadrian, and Nimble Robotics), supplemented by a broader universe of 8 private robotics firms and 1 public comparable.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, using total raised as a proxy base, applies a 1.9x multiplier typical of Series B advancement, yielding $241M. Peer-median valuation analysis across the 4-company cohort produces $1.6B, with a range spanning $1.0B to $1.8B. The latter method carries greater weight given direct stage and sector alignment of comparables.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $205M (low) to $1.9B (high), with a median of $933M. The wide dispersion reflects material uncertainty regarding Cambium's positioning relative to peers on growth trajectory, unit economics, and capital efficiency. The peer-median of $1.6B likely represents the most defensible point estimate, though confidence narrows materially only with access to Cambium's revenue, growth rate, and path to profitability relative to the comparable set.",
