      "narrative": "Fulfil is a Series B robotics and manufacturing company founded by Mir Aamir that has raised $127M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comparable universe of 9 private peers and 1 public company in the robotics and manufacturing sector, including Series B and adjacent-stage companies such as Bedrock Robotics ($1.8B), Dexterity ($1.6B), Hadrian ($1.6B), and Nimble Robotics ($1.0B).\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, which applies a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical of Series B advancement to the $127M raised proxy, yields $241M. Peer-median analysis across the 4 same-sector comparables produces $1.6B, with a range spanning $1.0B to $1.8B. The disparity between these methods reflects the meaningful gap between mechanistic capital-progression models and market-clearing multiples for proven operators in this stage cohort.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $205M to $1.9B, with a median of $933M. The wide range reflects material uncertainty around Fulfil's competitive positioning relative to peers, technology differentiation, and revenue trajectory\u2014factors not resolved by the capital-progression or peer-set methods alone. Further diligence on unit economics, customer concentration, and operational milestones would be required to narrow this range meaningfully.",
