      "narrative": "JITX, a Series A robotics and manufacturing company founded by Jonathan Bachrach, Duncan Haldane, Austin Buchan, and Patrick Li, is evaluated against a comparative universe of 9 private peers and 1 public comparable. Total capital raised to date is $12M.\n\nTwo valuation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis applies a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A advancement, yielding $24M. Peer-median analysis references three same-sector, same/adjacent-stage companies: Bedrock Robotics ($1.8B Series B), Dexterity ($1.6B Series B), and Walden Robotics ($1.1B Seed). The median valuation across this set is $1.6B, with a range spanning $1.1B to $1.8B.\n\nThe triangulated analysis produces a valuation range of $20.4M (low) to $1.9B (high), with a median of $837M. The wide dispersion reflects tension between two methodological anchors: stage-progression reasoning from actual capital deployed, versus peer benchmarking to more mature robotics entities. The stage-progression method is mechanically conservative and capital-centric; the peer-median reflects sector trading patterns but is less precise given JITX's earlier stage relative to most comparables. Key uncertainties include JITX's product maturity, addressable market definition, and whether peer valuations represent equilibrium or inflated sector multiples.",
