      "narrative": "Swan is a Seed-stage defense and security company that has raised $38.5M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a comp universe of 10 peers\u20142 public (DRSHF, IDEAFORGE.NS) and 8 private\u2014including same-sector Seed and Series A stage companies such as UFORCE ($1.0B), Singularity ($400M), and NODA AI ($125M).\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis uses the $38.5M total raised as a valuation proxy, applying a 2.5x step-up multiplier typical of Seed-to-next-stage progression, yielding $96M. Peer-median analysis across the 3 closest comparables (same sector, same/adjacent stage) produces a median valuation of $400M, with a range of $125M to $1.0B. The peer set reflects meaningful heterogeneity in stage and valuation outcomes within frontier defense tech.\n\nTriangulating both methods yields a valuation range of $82M (low) to $460M (high), with a median of $248M. The wide dispersion reflects two material uncertainties: first, the significant stage and valuation spread among early-stage defense-tech peers; second, Swan's nascent revenue profile relative to later-stage comps. The gap between stage-progression ($96M) and peer-median ($400M) suggests valuation outcome is highly sensitive to investor assessment of product-market fit and defensibility relative to the incumbent peer set.",
