      "narrative": "Perennial Autonomy is a Defense & Security stage company backed by Schmidt and prior employees from SpaceX, Google, and Apple, with $500M in government IDIQ contract value. The comparable universe includes 2 public peers (DRSHF, IDEAFORGE.NS) and 8 private companies in the sector, with top private peers including Anduril Industries, Helsing, Shield AI, Saronic, and Quantum-Systems.\n\nPeer-median valuation is not applicable here. The Defense & Security sector contains 21 same-sector peers overall, but filtering by stage, adjacency, and valuation tier yields fewer than the three datapoints required for a robust median comparison. A cross-sector median would introduce substantial noise given the capital intensity, regulatory environment, and contract dynamics specific to defense technology.\n\nWithout sufficient same-stage comparables, valuation hinges on forward cash flow visibility from the $500M IDIQ contract\u2014a material anchor point distinct from equity-stage fundraising. Key uncertainties include: (1) revenue recognition timing and drawdown rate against the contract ceiling; (2) margin structure under government cost accounting; (3) whether comparable public and private valuations reflect similar contract scale and customer concentration. Any valuation should be stress-tested against these contract execution risks rather than relying on peer multiples alone.",
