      "narrative": "Sereact, a Series B robotics and manufacturing company founded by Ralf Gulde and Marc Tuscher, has raised $140M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comparable universe of 9 private robotics firms and 1 public peer, with primary focus on 4 same-sector peers at Series B or Series C stage: Bedrock Robotics ($1.8B), Dexterity ($1.6B), Hadrian ($1.6B), and Nimble Robotics ($1.0B).\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, using $140M in total raised as a proxy for post-money valuation and applying a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical of Series B advancement, implies a valuation of $266M. Peer-median analysis across the four comparables yields a median valuation of $1.6B, with a range spanning $1.0B to $1.8B. The peer set reflects meaningful diversity in stage (two Series B, two Series C) and recent market valuations in the robotics sector.\n\nTriangulating both methods produces a valuation range of $226M (low) to $1.9B (high), with a median of $946M. The wide spread reflects material uncertainty regarding Sereact's positioning relative to peers\u2014specifically, whether the company's traction and technology justify peer-level valuations or whether stage-based progression better reflects current market conditions. Resolution of this gap requires clarity on revenue, growth metrics, and competitive differentiation relative to the peer set.",
