      "narrative": "Dyna Robotics, a Series A robotics and manufacturing company founded by Lindon Gao, York Yang, and Jason Ma, has raised $120M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comp universe of 9 private robotics firms and 1 public comparable, with peer valuations ranging from $1.1B to $1.8B across seed through Series B stages.\n\nTwo triangulation methods yield quantifiable benchmarks. The Stage-Progression method applies a 2.0x step-up multiplier to the $120M total raised, implying a $240M valuation. The Peer-Median approach uses three same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables\u2014Bedrock Robotics ($1.8B, Series B), Dexterity ($1.6B, Series B), and Walden Robotics ($1.1B, Seed)\u2014generating a median valuation of $1.6B with a range of $1.1B to $1.8B.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $204M to $1.9B, with a median of $945M. This wide range reflects material uncertainty in stage-adjustment methodologies and peer selection timing. The Stage-Progression method anchors toward the lower bound, while the Peer-Median approach is substantially elevated, likely reflecting either significant value creation post-funding or favorable market conditions in the robotics sector. Key uncertainties include recent revenue or growth metrics, the timing of peer valuations relative to current market conditions, and whether Series A positioning justifies median peer valuations of $1.6B given heterogeneity across robotics subsectors.",
