      "narrative": "Walden Robotics is a Seed-stage robotics and manufacturing company led by co-founder and CEO Russ Tedrake, an MIT professor and former SVP of Large Behavior Models at Toyota Research Institute. The company carries a last post-money valuation of $1.1B on $300M raised to date. The comp universe consists of 9 private robotics firms (including Divergent at $2.3B, Exotec at $2.0B, Locus Robotics at $2.0B, Bedrock Robotics at $1.8B, and Dexterity at $1.6B) and 1 public comparable.\n\nTwo valuation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, using a 2.5x step-up multiplier typical for Seed-to-next-stage advancement, implies $2.8B. Peer-median analysis across 7 same-sector, similar-valuation-tier comparables yields $1.8B, with a peer range of $1.0B to $2.3B. The peer cohort spans Series B through Series F, providing reasonable cross-stage reference points.\n\nTriangulation of these two methods supports a valuation range of $1.5B (low) to $3.2B (high), with a median of $2.2B. The current $1.1B valuation sits materially below the low-end estimate, suggesting either significant founder-specific value attribution or valuation conservatism. Key uncertainties include revenue traction, product-market fit maturity, and capital efficiency relative to peer benchmarks at later stages.",
